hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","1203 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is your chief, O Banu Ubayd? They said: al-Jadd ibn Qays, though there is miserliness in him. He said: What disease is more diseased than miserliness; rather your chief is Bishr ibn al-Bara ibn Ma'rur."
"1202","1204 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, who said: When Allah Almighty granted Khaybar as conquest to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and those of them who were killed were killed, Zaynab bint al-Harith the Jewess, and she was the daughter of the brother of Marhab, gifted a roasted sheep, and put poison in it, increasing it in the shoulder and the foreleg when she was told that they were the most beloved parts of the sheep to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, with him Bishr ibn al-Bara ibn Ma'rur, brother of Banu Salima, she presented it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he took the shoulder and the foreleg and bit from them, and Bishr took another bone and bit from it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chewed, Bishr chewed what was in his mouth, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lift your hands, for the shoulder of the sheep informs me that treachery has been done in it. So Bishr ibn al-Bara said: By the One who honoured you, I found that in the bite I ate, but what prevented me from spitting it out was only that I disliked spoiling your food. When you ate what was in your mouth, I did not wish to value my life above yours, and I hoped that I had not swallowed it while there was treachery in it. So Bishr did not rise from his place until his colour became like a Taylasan, and his pain lingered from it, until he could move only as he was moved. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained after, three years, until his illness in which he died came."
"1203","109 - Bishr ibn Suhaym al-Ghifari. 1205 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym al-Ghifari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us in the days of al-Tashriq and said: These are days of eating and drinking."
"1204","1206 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, and Daran ibn Sufyan ibn Mu'awiya al-Qattan, and al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter Paradise except a believing soul, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking."
"1205","1207 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Yahya al-Ushnani narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, who said: The days of Mina are days of eating and drinking."
"1206","1208 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Uqba narrated to us, from Hamza al-Zayyat, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"1207","1209 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Harun ibn Antara narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us in the days of al-Tashriq and said: None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and these days are days of eating and drinking."
"1208","1210 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us in the days of al-Tashriq and said: None shall enter Paradise except a believing soul, and these are days of eating and drinking."
"1209","1211 - al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in the days of Mina and said: None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and these are days of eating and drinking, so do not fast them."
"1210","1212 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, and Ibrahim ibn Ma'dan al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani narrated to us, both saying: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and these are days of eating and drinking, the days of Mina."
"1211","1213 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to announce in the days of al-Tashriq: Paradise shall be entered by none except a believer, and they are days of eating and drinking."
"1212","1214 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to announce in the days of al-Tashriq: None shall enter Paradise except a believer; they are days of eating and drinking."
"1213","1215 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, and al-Hajjaj, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he announced in Mina in the days of al-Tashriq: None shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul, and they are days of eating and drinking."
"1214","110 - Bishr al-Ghanawi. 1216 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-Mughira al-Ma'afiri, Abdullah ibn Bishr al-Ghanawi narrated to me, my father narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Constantinople shall surely be conquered, and excellent is the commander, its commander, and excellent is the army, that army. So Maslama ibn Abd al-Malik called me and asked me about this hadith, and I narrated it to him, and he campaigned that year."
"1215","111 - Bishr ibn Isma. 1217 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Jarir ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Mujja'a ibn Mihsan al-Abdi narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Husayn, from Bishr ibn Isma, Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Azd are from me and I am from them; I am angry for them when they are angry, and I am pleased for them when they are pleased. So Mu'awiya, may Allah have mercy on him, said: He said that only for Quraysh. So Bishr said: Shall I lie against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? If I lied against him I would have assigned it to my own people."
"1216","112 - Bishr, Abu Khalifa. 1218 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Ba'labakki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar al-Bara narrated to us, al-Nawwar bint Umar narrated to me, saying: Fatima bint Muslim narrated to me, saying: Khalifa ibn Bishr narrated to me, from his father Bishr, that he embraced Islam, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to him his wealth and his children. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him and saw him and his son Talq tied together with a rope, and said: What is this, O Bishr? He said: I vowed that if Allah returned to me my wealth and my children, I would surely perform Hajj to the House of Allah tied together. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the rope and cut it, and said to them both: Perform Hajj, for this is from Satan."
"1217","113 - Bishr ibn Asim. 1219 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sayyar Abu al-Hakam narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salama, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, appointed Bishr ibn Asim over the charities of Hawazin, but Bishr stayed back. So Umar met him and said: What kept you back; do we not have hearing and obedience upon you? He said: Yes, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is put in charge of anything of the affairs of the Muslims will be brought on the Day of Resurrection until he is made to stand upon the bridge of Hell; if he was a doer of good he will pass, and if he was a doer of evil the bridge will break with him and he will fall into it for seventy autumns. He said: So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, went out gloomy and grieved, and Abu Dharr met him and said: Why do I see you gloomy and grieved? He said: What prevents me from being gloomy and grieved, when I heard Bishr ibn Asim saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is put in charge of anything of the affairs of the Muslims will be brought on the Day of Resurrection until he is made to stand upon the bridge of Hell; if he was a doer of good he will pass, and if he was a doer of evil the bridge will break with him and he will fall into it for seventy autumns. Abu Dharr said: And did you not hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: No. He said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is put in charge of anyone of the people will be brought on the Day of Resurrection until he is made to stand upon the bridge of Hell; if he was a doer of good he will pass, and if he was a doer of evil the bridge will break with him and he will fall into it for seventy autumns, and it is black and dark. So which of the two hadiths pains your heart more? He said: Both have pained my heart. So who will take it with what it entails? And Abu Dharr said: The one whose nose Allah cuts off and whose cheek He sticks to the ground; indeed we know only good, and perhaps if you entrust it to one who does not act justly in it, you will not be saved from its sin."
"1218","Chapter of those named Bashir. 114 - Bashir ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, Abu al-Nu'man, of al-Aqaba, of Badr. 1220 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of the companions of al-Aqaba among the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Bashir ibn Sa'd, and he witnessed Badr."
"1219","1221 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, from Banu Zayd ibn Malik ibn Tha'laba ibn Ka'b ibn al-Khazraj ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Bashir ibn Sa'd ibn Tha'laba ibn Julas."
"1220","1222 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Regarding the naming of the companions of al-Aqaba among the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Bashir ibn Sa'd, Abu al-Nu'man."
"1221","1223 - Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Abu Suhayl Nafi' ibn Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Bashir ibn Sa'd, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The position of the believer to the believer is the position of the head to the body; whenever the body complains, the head complains for it, and whenever the head complains, the rest of the body complains."
"1222","1224 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Darrab al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Makhrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: May Allah have mercy on a servant who hears my saying and memorises it, for many a carrier of understanding is not understanding, and many a carrier of understanding conveys it to one more understanding than him. Three things over which the heart of a believer does not harbour deceit: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere counsel to the rulers of the Muslims, and adhering to the congregation of the Muslims."
"1223","115 - Bashir al-Aslami, Abu Bishr. 1225 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Bashir al-Aslami, from his father, who had companionship with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this plant, let him not approach our mosque, meaning garlic."
"1224","1226 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Bazzar al-Asbahani narrated to us, both saying: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Abu Mas'ud, meaning Abd al-A'la ibn Abi al-Musawir al-Jarrar, from Abu Salama Bishr ibn Bashir al-Aslami, from his father, who said: When the Emigrants came to Medina, they found the water disagreeable, and a man of Banu Ghifar owned a spring called Ruma, and he used to sell from it a waterskin for a mudd. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Sell it to me for a spring in Paradise. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing besides it for me and my family; I cannot do that. That reached Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, so he bought it for thirty-five thousand dirhams, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, will you grant me the same as you granted him, a spring in Paradise, if I buy it? He said: Yes. He said: I have bought it and made it for the Muslims."
"1225","116 - Bashir ibn Uqraba al-Juhani, also known as Abu al-Yaman. 1227 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hujr ibn al-Harith al-Ghassani narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Awf al-Kinani, who was an agent of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz over al-Ramla, that he witnessed Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan saying to Bashir ibn Uqraba al-Juhani on the day Amr ibn Sa'id was killed: O Abu al-Yaman, I need your speech, so speak. So Bashir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever delivers a sermon seeking thereby nothing but show and repute, Allah Almighty will make him stand in a station of show and repute."
"1226","1228 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zur'a, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Bashir ibn Uqraba al-Juhani, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever delivers a sermon seeking thereby nothing but show and repute, Allah Almighty will make him stand in a station of show and repute."
"1227","117 - Bashir al-Sulami. 1229 - Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Isa ibn Ali al-Ansari narrated to us, from Rafi' ibn Bashir al-Sulami, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A fire is about to come out illuminating the necks of camels at Busra, moving at the pace of slow camels, travelling by day and resting by night, going in the morning and returning in the evening. It will be said: The fire has gone in the morning, O people, so go in the morning; the fire has said at midday, O people, so rest at midday; it has gone in the evening, O people, so go in the evening. Whoever it overtakes, it will consume him."
"1228","118 - Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyya al-Sadusi, and he is Bashir ibn Ma'bad ibn Sharahil ibn Sab' ibn Sabbar, a Sadusi, and his name in the pre-Islamic period was Zahm, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Bashir. 1230 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, Khalid ibn Sumayr narrated to us, Bashir ibn Nahik narrated to us, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyya, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and his name in the pre-Islamic period was Zahm, then he emigrated, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Bashir - said: While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to me: O son of al-Khasasiyya, what grievance have you against Allah this morning? He said: I have no grievance against Allah this morning for anything; all good He has done for me. He said: Then he came upon the graves of the Muslims and said: These have attained much good, saying it three times. Then he came upon the graves of the polytheists and said: These have missed much good, saying it three times. Then a glance came from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was a man walking over the graves wearing two sandals, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called to him: O wearer of the two Sibti sandals, remove your sandals. The man looked, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the man removed his sandals and threw them away. And the wording is that of the hadith of Muslim."
"1229","1231 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, from his father, from Layla, wife of Bashir, who said: I used to fast continuously without breaking, so Bashir forbade me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me from this, saying: Only the Christians do that. But fast as Allah Almighty commanded, then complete the fast until night, and when night comes, break fast."
"1230","1232 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, both saying: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, saying: I heard Layla, wife of Bashir, saying: Bashir informed me that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I fast on Friday and do not speak to anyone that day. He said: Do not fast on Friday except in days of which it is the last, and as for not speaking to anyone, by my life, that you speak and enjoin good and forbid evil is better than that you remain silent."
"1231","1233 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Jabala ibn Suhaym, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Abdi, from Ibn al-Khasasiyya al-Sadusi, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him, and he stipulated upon me: You bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and you pray the five, and fast Ramadan, and pay zakat, and perform Hajj to the House, and strive in the path of Allah. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, as for two of them I cannot bear them: zakat, for by Allah I have nothing but ten she-camels, they are the support of my family and their mounts; and as for jihad, they claim that whoever turns back has incurred anger from Allah, and I fear that when fighting comes upon me, my soul will become humble and dislike death. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grasped his hand and moved it, then said: No charity and no jihad - will you enter Paradise? So I pledged allegiance to him upon all of them."
"1232","1234 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Jabala ibn Suhaym, from Mu'thir ibn Afara, who said: I stayed in the house of a man of Abd al-Qays called Ibn al-Khasasiyya, and Ibn al-Khasasiyya narrated to us, saying: I said, O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall I pledge allegiance to you? And he mentioned the hadith."
"1233","1235 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ayyash ibn al-Walid al-Raqqam narrated to us, and Abdan narrated to us, Azhar ibn Marwan al-Raqqashi narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatada, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyya, who said: And our companions narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, narrating from his Lord Almighty: Fasting is a shield; My servant shields himself with it from the Fire. And fasting is for Me, and I reward for it. He leaves his food and his desire for My sake. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, the changed breath of the mouth of the fasting person with Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection is more pleasant than the scent of musk."
"1234","1236 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi and Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, both saying: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Uqba ibn al-Mughira al-Shaybani narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from his father, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyya, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and caught up with him at al-Baqi', and I heard him saying: Peace be upon the people of the abodes among the believers. And my sandal strap broke, so he said to me: Mend your foot? I said: O Messenger of Allah, my absence has been long and I am far from the abode of my people. He said: O Bashir, will you not praise the One who took your forelock from among Rabi'a, a people who think that were it not for them the earth would collapse with those upon it."
"1235","119 - Bashir al-Muharibi. 1237 - Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar, from Ayyub ibn Bashir, from his father, who said: There was a disturbance among Banu Mu'awiya, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to make peace between them. Then he turned to a grave and said: You do not know. So he was asked about it, and he said: He is being questioned about me, and he said: I do not know."
"1236","120 - Bashir ibn Yazid al-Duba'i. 1238 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, al-Ashhab al-Duba'i narrated to me, Bashir ibn Yazid al-Duba'i narrated to me, who had reached the pre-Islamic period, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Dhi Qar: This is the first day in which the Arabs obtained justice from the non-Arabs."
"1237","121 - Bashir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, martyred on the day of al-Yamama. 1239 - Muhammad Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of those killed on the day of al-Yamama among the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Bashir ibn Abdullah."
"1238","123 - Bayhara ibn Amir. 1240 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Rashid narrated to us, al-Rahhal ibn al-Mundhir al-Umari narrated to us, my father narrated to me that he heard his father Bayhara ibn Amir saying: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and embraced Islam, and we asked him to relieve us of al-Atama. He said: The prayer of al-Atama. So we said: We are occupied with milking our camels. He said: You, if Allah wills, will milk and pray."
"1239","124 - Buhayr ibn al-Haytham al-Ansari, of al-Aqaba. 1241 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqaba among the Ansar, then from Banu Haritha ibn al-Harith: Buhayr ibn al-Haytham."
"1240","125 - Bahz. 1242 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Massisi and Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn Adi narrated to us, Thubayt ibn Kathir al-Basri al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Bahz, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to brush his teeth horizontally, drink by sipping, breathe three times, and say: It is more wholesome, more digestible, and healthier."
"1241","126 - Basra ibn Abi Basra al-Ghifari, also called Nadra, and the correct is Basra. 1243 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi al-Basri narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Basra, who said: I married a virgin woman in her chamber and found her pregnant. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for the child, he is your servant; when she gives birth, flog her one hundred, and she has the dowry for what was made lawful of her private part."
"1242","127 - Basbas al-Juhani, of Badr, ally of Banu Tarif ibn al-Khazraj al-Ansari. 1244 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then from Banu Tarif ibn al-Khazraj: Basbas al-Juhani, their ally."
"1243","1245 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, from Banu Sa'ida ibn Ka'b ibn al-Khazraj: Basbas al-Juhani, an ally of theirs."
"1244","128 - Bujayr ibn Abi Bujayr al-Ansari, of Badr. 1246 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then from Banu Dinar ibn al-Najjar: Bujayr ibn Bujayr, an ally of theirs."
"1245","Chapter of Ta. 129 - Tamim ibn Aws al-Dari, also said Ibn Qays, known as Abu Ruqayya, and he is the uncle of Tamim ibn Aws ibn Kharija ibn Sawwad ibn Jadhima ibn Dira' ibn Adi ibn al-Dar ibn Lakhm ibn Habib ibn Numara ibn Lakhm. 1247 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ilyas, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The first who lit a lamp in the mosque was Tamim al-Dari."
"1246","1248 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatada, from Ibn Sirin: That Tamim al-Dari bought a garment for a thousand and used to pray in it."
"1247","1249 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Tamim al-Dari sought permission from Umar for storytelling, but he refused to permit him. Then he sought his permission and he refused to permit him. Then he sought his permission and he said: If you wish - and he gestured with his hand, meaning slaughter."
"1248","1250 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, who said: A man of the people of Mecca said to me: This is the standing place of your brother Tamim al-Dari. I saw him stand a night until morning, or nearly morning, reciting a verse of the Book of Allah Almighty, bowing, prostrating and weeping: Or do those who commit evils think that We will make them like those who believe and do righteous deeds, equal in their life and their death? Evil is what they judge."
"1249","1251 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq: That Tamim al-Dari repeated this verse until morning: Or do those who commit evils think - the verse."
"1250","What Tamim al-Dari narrated with a chain. 1252 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, Zayd ibn Waqid informed me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murra, from Tamim al-Dari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night, standing in worship for a night will be written for him."
"1251","1253 - Musa ibn Khazim al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Fadala ibn Ubayd and Tamim al-Dari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever recites ten verses in a night, a qintar will be written for him, and a qintar is better than the world and what is in it. When the Day of Resurrection comes, your Lord Almighty will say: Recite and ascend, a degree for each verse, until he ends at the last verse with him. Your Lord Almighty will say to the servant: Take hold. The servant will say with his hand: O Lord, You know best. So He will say: With this, eternity, and with this, bliss."
"1252","1254 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla, from Rawh ibn Zinba', who said: I visited Tamim al-Dari while he was governor over Bayt al-Maqdis, cleaning barley for his horse. So I said: O commander, did you have none to suffice you this? He said: No; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever cleans barley for his horse, then stands with it until he feeds it to him, Allah writes for him a good deed for every grain of barley."
"1253","1255 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing the servant will be reckoned for is the prayer, then the rest of the deeds."
"1254","1256 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing the servant will be reckoned for is the prayer, then the rest of the deeds."
"1255","1257 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Dirar, from Abu Abdullah al-Shami, from Tamim al-Dari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Friday is obligatory except upon a woman, or a boy, or a sick person, or a slave, or a traveller."
"1256","1258 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan al-Nahdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to us, from al-Hakam Abu Amr, from Dirar ibn Amr, from Abu Abdullah al-Shami, from Tamim al-Dari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The right of the husband upon the wife is that she not abandon his bed, and that she fulfil his oath, and obey his command, and not go out except with his permission, and not admit upon him one whom he dislikes."
"1257","1259 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani, and Ali ibn Jabala al-Asbahani narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Dumayra narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Tamim al-Dari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every ambiguous matter is forbidden, and there is no ambiguity in religion."
"1258","1260 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is only sincere counsel, religion is only sincere counsel, religion is only sincere counsel. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom? He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to the leaders of the believers, and to their common folk."
"1259","1261 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih al-Samman, from Ata ibn Yazid of Banu Layth, from Tamim al-Dari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the Muslims and the believers, and to their common folk."
"1260","1262 - al-Husayn ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, who said: I heard Ata ibn Yazid narrating from Tamim al-Dari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Religion is sincere counsel, three times. I said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk."
"1261","1263 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isma'il al-Talqani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar used to narrate to us from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Ata ibn Yazid. Sufyan said: So I met his son Suhayl and said: Did you hear from your father a hadith narrated to us by Amr ibn Dinar from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim from Abu Salih? He said: I heard it from the one who narrated it to my father from him: I heard Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi narrating from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere counsel, three times. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to His Prophet, and to the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk."
"1262","1264 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, that Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Tamim al-Dari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the Muslims and their community."
"1263","1265 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam informed us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere counsel. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk."
"1264","1266 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: Zuhayr Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yazid, who said: I heard Tamim al-Dari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere counsel, three times. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah and His Book, and to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the believers and their common folk."
"1265","1267 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere counsel, three times. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His angels, and to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the believers or the Muslims, and their common folk."
"1266","1268 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abdullah ibn Zurara al-Raqqi narrated to me, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His Messenger, and to His Book, and to the leaders of the believers, and to the believers in general."
"1267","1269 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, and Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Usama Abdullah ibn Usama al-Kalbi narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Umar ibn Yazid al-Hamdani narrated to us, from his grandfather, from Fatima bint Qays, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tayba is Medina, and there is no mountain pass of its passes except upon it an angel brandishing his sword; the Dajjal shall never enter it. And Abu Kurayb said: Uthman ibn Zayd."
"1268","1270 - Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu Ubayda al-Askari narrated to us, Sayf ibn Miskin narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Fatima bint Qays, who said: I heard the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling: Prayer in congregation. So I went out among women of the Ansar until we came to the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us the noon prayer, then ascended the pulpit and faced us laughing, then said: By Allah, I gathered you not for a new desire nor for fear, but for a hadith narrated to me by Tamim al-Dari, who came to me, embraced Islam and pledged allegiance. He informed me that he boarded with thirty men of Lakhm and Judham, two tribes of the tribes of the Arabs of Yemen, and they encountered the sea when it was agitated, so the waves played with them for a month, then cast them near sunset upon an island of the islands of the sea. Then we were met by a hairy beast whose front could not be distinguished from its back. We said: What are you, O beast? So it spoke to us by Allah's permission with a fluent eloquent tongue, saying: I am al-Jassasa. We said: What is al-Jassasa? It said: Away from me; upon you is that monastery at the far end of the island, for in it is a man most eager for your news. So we came to the monastery, and there we were met by a man, the greatest man I ever saw in creation and the stoutest in body, with his right eye wiped out, as if his eye were phlegm on a plastered wall, with his hands chained to his neck, and his legs bound with shackles from his knees to his feet. So we said to him: What are you, O man? He said: As for my news, you have come upon it, but inform me of your news: what cast you upon this island? And this island, no human has reached it since I came to it. So he said to us: Inform me of the Lake of Tiberias, what has become of it? We said to him: About which of its matters do you ask? He said: Has its water receded? And have wonders begun in it? We said to him: No. He said: It will be. Then he was silent a while, then said: Inform me of the spring of Zughar, what has become of it? We said to him: About which of its matters? He said: Do its people cultivate upon it? We said to him: Yes. He said: It will be that its water will sink and its people will not cultivate upon it. Then he was silent a while, then said: Inform me of the palms of Baysan, what has become of them? We said to him: About which of their matters do you ask? He said: Do they bear fruit? We said to him: Yes. He said: They will not bear fruit. Then he was silent a while, then said: Inform me of the unlettered Prophet, what has become of him? We said to him: About which of his matters do you ask? He said: Has he appeared yet? We said: Yes. He said: What did the Arabs do with him? We said: Among them are those who fought him, and among them are those who believed him. So he said: Whoever believed him is better for him - three times. So we said: Inform us of your news, O man. So he said: Do you not know me? We said: Had we known you, we would not have asked you. He said: I am the Dajjal. It is near that I will be permitted to come out. When I come out, I will tread all the islands of the Arabs except Mecca and Tayba; whenever I intend them, an angel with a drawn sword meets me and turns me away from them. Abu al-Ashhab said: Amir said: Fatima said: So I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, then he said: Shall I not inform you that this is Tayba - three times - then he said: Shall I not inform you that he is toward Syria. Then he fainted for a while, then trembled, then it was lifted from him, then he said: Rather he is in Yemen - three times - then he fainted for a while, trembled, then it was lifted from him, and he said: Rather he is toward Iraq, rather he is toward Iraq, rather he is toward Iraq. He will come out when he comes out from a town called Asbahan, from one of its villages called Rastqabadh. He will come out when he comes out with seventy thousand at his vanguard wearing garments of coarse cloth, with him two rivers, a river of water and a river of fire. Whoever of you reaches that, and is told: Enter the water, let him not enter it, for it is fire; and when he is told: Enter the fire, let him enter it, for it is water."
"1269","1271 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Amr ibn Mansur al-Mashriqi narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatima bint Qays, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal, saying: From the direction of Iraq he is, not from the direction of Syria he is - and he mentioned the hadith."
"1270","1272 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibn Mawhab, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man embraces Islam at my hands then dies. He said: You are the most entitled of people to his life and his death."
"1271","1273 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, both saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrating to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Sunna regarding a man of the people of disbelief who embraces Islam at the hands of a man of the Muslims? He said: He is the most entitled of people to his life and his death."
"1272","1274 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Anbari narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man of the polytheists embraces Islam at the hands of a man of the Muslims? He said: He is the most entitled of people to his life and his death."
"1273","1275 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Tamim al-Dari, that he used to gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every year a waterskin of wine. When the year it was forbidden came, he gifted him a waterskin, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: It has been forbidden. He said: Shall I sell it? He said: Its purchase and its price are forbidden."
"1274","1276 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Some people cut off the humps of camels and cut the tails of sheep. He said: Whatever is cut from a living animal is dead meat."
"1275","1277 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, some people cut off the humps of camels and the tails of sheep while they are alive. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is dead meat."
"1276","1278 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Isa ibn Hammad Zughba narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Khalil ibn Murra, from al-Azhar ibn Abdullah al-Himsi, from Tamim al-Dari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, the One, the Unique, the Eternal, who has taken neither companion nor child, and there is none comparable to Him, ten times, Allah writes for him forty thousand good deeds."
"1277","1279 - Ahmad ibn Ma Bahram al-Idhaji narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: I requested from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a land in Syria before it was conquered, and he gave it to me. Then Umar conquered it in his time, so I came to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me a land, from such-and-such to such-and-such. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, made a third of it for the wayfarer, a third for its cultivation, and a third for us."
"1278","1280 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Afiya ibn Ayyub informed me, my grandfather narrated to me, Mu'awiya ibn Salih narrated to me, that Abu Yahya Sulaym ibn Amir al-Khabairi narrated to him, from Tamim al-Dari, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This religion shall surely reach what the night reaches, until it enters the house of mud and the house of hair, until Allah honours Islam thereby and humiliates disbelief. Tamim said: I recognised that in my household: whoever of them embraced Islam attained good, honour and might, and whoever of them remained upon disbelief attained humiliation, abasement and jizya."
"1279","1281 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Tamim al-Dari informed, or I was informed of him, that Tamim al-Dari prayed two rak'as after Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, forbade prayer after Asr. So he came to him and struck him with the stick. So Tamim gestured to him to sit while he was in his prayer, and Umar sat until Tamim finished. Then he said to Umar: Why did you strike me? He said: Because you prayed these two rak'as when I had forbidden them. He said: I prayed them with one better than you, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I do not mean you, O people, but I fear that after you will come people who pray between Asr and Maghrib until they pass through the hour in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer, as they joined between Zuhr and Asr, then they will say: We saw so-and-so and so-and-so praying after Asr."
"1280","130 - Abu Rifa'a al-Adawi, whose name is Tamim ibn Usayd. 1282 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Ma'ni narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, who said: Abu Rifa'a used to heat water for his companions, then say: Perform ablution well from this, for I shall perform better than this, and he would perform ablution with cold water."
"1281","1283 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us, Abu Zafar Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, who said: Sila ibn Ashyam said: Abu Rifa'a was afflicted, and we were on a campaign, and I saw as if I saw Abu Rifa'a upon a swift she-camel, while I was upon a slow camel, following his tracks. Then he would rein her in until I said: Now I will make him hear my voice, then he would let her go and she would speed off, and I would follow him. So I interpreted my dream that it is the path of Abu Rifa'a I take, while I toil in deed after him with toil."
"1282","1284 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, who said: Abu Rifa'a al-Adawi said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, a stranger has come asking about his religion, not knowing what his religion is? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, leaving his sermon, then a chair whose legs I thought were of iron was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended it, and began teaching me from what Allah taught him. Then he went to his sermon and completed it."
"1283","131 - Tamim ibn Zayd, Abu Abbad al-Ansari, then al-Mazini. 1285 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution: he began and washed his face and his forearms, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then wiped his head."
"1284","1286 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe with water over his beard and his feet."
"1285","133 - Tamim ibn Abd Amr, Abu al-Hasan al-Mazini, who was an agent of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, over Medina when he went out to him, Sahl ibn Hunayf. 1287 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Abu al-Hasan al-Mazini said: The grandfather of Amr ibn Yahya, his name is Tamim ibn Amr; Ali ibn Abi Talib appointed him over Medina when he went out to Iraq, when Sahl ibn Hunayf went out to him."
"1286","134 - Tamim ibn Ya'ar al-Ansari, then al-Khudri, of Badr. 1288 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then from Banu Khudra ibn Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Tamim ibn Ya'ar ibn Qays ibn Adi."
"1287","1289 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Tamim ibn Ya'ar ibn Qays ibn Adi ibn Umayya."
"1288","135 - Tamim, freedman of Banu Ghanm ibn al-Salm ibn Malik ibn al-Aws ibn Haritha, of Badr. 1290 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar: Tamim, freedman of Banu Ghanm ibn al-Salm ibn Malik ibn al-Aws ibn Haritha."
"1289","1291 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar: Tamim, freedman of Banu Ghanm ibn al-Salm ibn Malik ibn al-Aws."
"1290","136 - Tamim, freedman of Khirash ibn al-Simma al-Ansari, of Badr. 1292 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar: Tamim, freedman of Khirash ibn al-Simma."
"1291","1293 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then of al-Khazraj, then of Banu Salima: Tamim, freedman of Khirash ibn al-Simma."
"1292","137 - Tamim ibn al-Harith ibn Qays al-Qurashi al-Sahmi, killed on the day of Ajnadayn. 1294 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Ajnadayn among the Muslims, then of Quraysh, then of Banu Sahm ibn Husays: Tamim ibn al-Harith ibn Qays."
"1293","1295 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Ajnadayn of Quraysh, then of Banu Sahm: Tamim ibn al-Harith ibn Qays."
"1294","138 - Talib ibn Taghlib al-Anbari, also said Talibb with doubling of the ba. 1296 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Harami ibn Hafs al-Qasmal narrated to us, Ghalib ibn Hujra narrated to me, Umm Abdullah bint Milqam narrated to me, from her father, from her grandfather al-Talibb, that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would feed me and measure for me a mudd, so I would lift it and eat with the people, until there was food. He said: And al-Talibb came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You fed me a mudd on such-and-such day, and I gathered it until today. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed it from him, and he had from him what he used to measure for him before that."
"1295","1297 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqqashi narrated to us, both saying: Ghalib ibn Hujra narrated to us, Umm Abdullah bint Milqam narrated to me, from her father, from her grandfather al-Talibb, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hospitality is three days, a binding right; whatever is after that is charity."
"1296","1298 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Ghalib ibn Hujra narrated to us, Milqam ibn al-Talibb narrated to me, that al-Talibb narrated to him that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. So he said: When permission is given to you, or until permission is given to you. He said: So he waited as long as Allah willed, then he called him, wiped his hand upon his face, and said: O Allah, forgive al-Talibb and have mercy on him - three times."
"1297","1299 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Ghalib ibn Hujra narrated to us, saying: I heard Milqam ibn al-Talibb narrating from his father, who said: I accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I did not hear any prohibition of the insects of the earth."
"1298","1300 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Bishr al-Anbari, from Ibn al-Talibb, from his father: That a man freed something of his of a slave, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not hold him liable."
"1299","139 - Tammam ibn al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. 1301 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisa ibn Uqba narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ali al-Sayqal, from Ja'far, seller of striped garments, from Ja'far ibn Tamim ibn al-Abbas, or Ibn Tammam ibn al-Abbas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How is it I see you coming to me with yellowed teeth; use the siwak. Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have made the siwak obligatory upon them as prayer was made obligatory upon them."
"1300","1302 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ali al-Sayqal, freedman of Banu Asad, from Ja'far ibn Tammam ibn Abbas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How is it you enter upon me with yellowed teeth; use the siwak. Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them with the siwak at every purification."
"1301","1303 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ali al-Sayqal, from Ja'far ibn Tammam ibn al-Abbas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How is it you enter upon me with yellowed teeth; use the siwak. Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer."
"1302","140 - al-Tayyihan. 1304 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ishaq said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in his march to Khaybar to Amir ibn al-Akwa', and the name of al-Akwa' was Sinan: Take for us from your songs. So he dismounted chanting rajaz for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1303","Chapter of Tha, those named Thabit. 141 - Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas al-Ansari. 1305 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of those killed on the day of al-Yamama among the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas."
"1304","1306 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas was martyred that day, in the year twelve."
"1305","1307 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Thabit ibn Qays came on the day of al-Yamama, having perfumed himself with hanut and spread his shrouds, and said: O Allah, I disavow to You what these have brought, and I apologise for what these have done. So he was killed, and he had a coat of mail which was stolen. Then a man saw him in a dream, saying: My coat of mail is in a pot under the fireplace, in such-and-such place, and he counselled him with counsels. So they sought the coat of mail and found it, and they executed the counsels."
"1306","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Qatan ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Thabit ibn Qays was the orator (khatib) of the Ansar."
"1307","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Azhar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, who said: Thumama ibn Abdillah ibn Anas informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, so a man said: I know his news, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He went to him and found him in a house with his head bowed, weeping. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has missed you. He said: I raised my voice above the voice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so my deeds have been nullified, and I am among the people of the Fire. He went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him, so he said: Go back to him and inform him that he is not among the people of the Fire, and that he is among the people of Paradise."
"1308","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Thabit, from Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, that Thabit came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have feared that I am destroyed. He said: Why? He said: Allah forbade us to be praised for what we did not do, and I am a man who loves praise; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a loud-voiced man; and He forbade us pride, and I am a man who loves beauty. He said: O Thabit, would you not love to live praiseworthy and be killed as a martyr? So he was killed on the day of al-Yamama."
"1309","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, Abu Amr al-Awzai narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to me, Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas narrated to me, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have feared that I am destroyed. He said: In what? I said: Allah forbade a man to be praised for what he did not do, and I find I love praise; and Allah forbade pride, and I find I love pride; and Allah forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a loud-voiced man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you not pleased to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he lived praiseworthy and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylima."
"1310","Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have feared that I am destroyed. He said: In what? He said: Allah forbids us to be praised for what we did not do, and I find I love praise; and He forbade us pride, and I am a man who loves beauty; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a loud-voiced man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Thabit ibn Qays, are you not pleased to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise?"
"1311","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from Muawiya ibn Yahya, from al-Zuhri, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Ansari informed me, that Thabit ibn Qays al-Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, I have feared that I am destroyed. He said to him: Why? He said: Allah forbade a man to love to be praised for what he did not do, and I find I love praise; and He forbade us pride, and I find I love beauty; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a loud-voiced man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Thabit, are you not pleased to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he lived praiseworthy and was killed on the day of Musaylima."
"1312","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Anbasa narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, Ismail ibn Thabit informed, that Thabit ibn Qays al-Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, I have feared that I am destroyed. He said: Why? He said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, forbade us praise, that we be praised for what we did not do, and I love praise; and He forbade us pride, and I love beauty; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a loud-voiced man. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Thabit, are you not pleased to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he lived praiseworthy and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylima the Liar."
"1313","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Makhshi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, my maternal uncle al-Mughira ibn al-Hasan ibn Rashid al-Hashimi narrated to me, Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Salim narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas al-Ansari, that Thabit ibn Qays said: O Messenger of Allah, I have feared that I am destroyed. He said: Why? He said: Allah prevents a man from being praised for what he did not do, and I find I love praise; and He forbids pride, and I find I love beauty; and Allah forbids us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am loud-voiced. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Thabit, are you not pleased to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise?"
"1314","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu Thabit ibn Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas narrated to us, my father Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas narrated to me, from his father, who said: When this verse was revealed: Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, Thabit sat on the road weeping. Asim ibn Adi passed by him and said: What makes you weep, O Thabit? He said: I am loud-voiced and I fear this verse was revealed about me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O my son, are you not pleased to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise? He said: I accept the glad tidings of Allah and His Messenger; I will never raise my voice above the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then was revealed: Indeed those who lower their voices, the verse."
"1315","Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Thabit ibn Qays, who said: Pride was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was stern about it, and said: Indeed Allah does not love every arrogant boaster. A man among the people said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I wash my clothes and I admire their whiteness, and I admire my sandal straps and my whip handle. He said: That is not pride; pride is only to reject the truth and despise people."
"1316","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Wara narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother Isa, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas al-Ansari, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he recited this verse: Indeed Allah does not love every arrogant boaster. He mentioned pride and magnified it, so Thabit ibn Qays wept. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What makes you weep? He said: O Prophet of Allah, I love beauty, such that I admire even my sandal straps being fine. He said: Then you are among the people of Paradise; pride is not beautifying your mount and saddle, but pride is whoever rejects the truth and despises people."
"1317","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Jarrah ibn al-Minhal, from Ibn Ata ibn Abi Muslim al-Khurasani, from his father, from Abu Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, from his father, who said: I came to the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the salam, he turned to me while I was praying, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept looking at me while I prayed. When I finished, he said: Did you not pray with us? I said: Yes. He said: Then what is this prayer? I said: O Messenger of Allah, the two rakas of Fajr; I left my home and had not prayed them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not criticize me for that."
"1318","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to me, from Ata al-Khurasani, who said: I came to Medina and asked about someone who would narrate to me the hadith of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, so they directed me to his daughter. I asked her and she said: I heard my father say: When was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed Allah does not love every arrogant boaster, it weighed heavily on Thabit; he closed his door and began weeping. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed, so he sent for him and asked him; he told him what weighed heavily on him from it, and said: I am a man who loves beauty and to lead my people. He said: You are not among them; rather you will live well, die well, and Allah will admit you to Paradise. She said: Then when Allah revealed to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet and do not speak loudly to him, he did the same. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed, so he sent for him about what weighed heavily on him, that he is loud-voiced and fears he is among those whose deeds are nullified. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are not among them; rather you will live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and Allah will admit you to Paradise. When Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, mobilized the Muslims against the apostates and al-Yamama and Musaylima the Liar, Thabit ibn Qays marched among those who marched. When they met Musaylima and Banu Hanifa, the Muslims were defeated three times. Thabit and Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfa, said: Not thus did we fight with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They dug a pit for themselves, entered it, and fought until they were killed. She said: A Muslim man saw Thabit ibn Qays in a dream, and he said: When I was killed yesterday, a Muslim man passed by me and took a precious coat of mail from me; his dwelling is at the farthest part of the camp, and by his dwelling is a horse rearing in its tether; he has overturned a pot over the coat of mail and placed a saddle over the pot. Go to Khalid ibn al-Walid and let him send for my coat of mail and take it. When you come to the successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), inform him that I owe such-and-such debt, and I own such-and-such wealth, and so-and-so of my slaves is freed. Beware of saying this is a dream and neglecting it. He said: He went to Khalid ibn al-Walid, who sent for the coat of mail and found it as he described. He came to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and informed him, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, executed his will after his death. We do not know of anyone whose will was carried out after his death except Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1319","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from his brother Isa, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who hear from you."
"1320","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Musa ibn Anas, from his father, who said: I came upon Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas on the day of al-Yarmuk, and he had uncovered his thighs, saying: Thus, away from our faces, we strike the enemy; and evil is what you have accustomed your peers to. By Allah, not thus did we fight with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1321","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, and Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Said al-Hamdani narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he visited him and said: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, from Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas. Then he took dust from al-Batha in a cup containing water and poured it over him."
"1322","142 - Thabit ibn al-Dahhak ibn Khalifa al-Ansari, known as Abu Zayd. 1324 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills himself with poison will be punished with it; and whoever testifies against a Muslim, or he said against a believer, of disbelief, is like killing him; and whoever curses him is like killing him; and whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he swore."
"1323","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, and he had companionship - Hammad said: If I said it is raised (marfu) I would not care - who said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he said."
"1324","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he said; and whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it in the fire of Hell; and cursing the believer is like killing him; and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him."
"1325","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he said; and whoever slaughters himself with something will be slaughtered with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"1326","Al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"1327","Al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, and he had companionship, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills himself with something deliberately will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection in the fire of Hell; and whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying deliberately, is as he said; and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him; and whoever curses a believer is like killing him."
"1328","Abdullah ibn Umar al-Saffar al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bazigh narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursing the believer is like killing him; and whoever accuses a believing man or believing woman of disbelief is like killing him; and whoever swears by a religion other than Islam is as he said; and whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection; and a servant has no vow in what he does not own."
"1329","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in what one does not own; and cursing the believer is like killing him; and whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he said; and whoever says to a believer: O disbeliever, is like killing him."
"1330","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man has no vow in what he does not own; and cursing the believer is like killing him; and whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he said; and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him."
"1331","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bishr al-Hariri narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abu Qilaba informed him that Thabit ibn al-Dahhak informed him that he pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) under the tree, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he said; and whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection; and a man has no vow in what he does not own."
"1332","Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Qilaba narrated to me, Thabit ibn al-Dahhak narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he said; and whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection; and a man has no vow in what he does not own; and cursing the believer is like killing him; and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him."
"1333","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he said; and a man has no vow in what he does not own; and whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it in the Hereafter."
"1334","Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Abu Qilaba narrated to me, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, is as he said; and whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection; and a man has no vow in what he does not own."
"1335","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, both saying: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Qilaba narrated to me, that Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, among the companions of the tree, narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam is as he said; and the son of Adam has no vow in what he does not own; and whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever curses a believer is like killing him; and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him."
"1336","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal and Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, both saying: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, who said: The Messenger of Allah said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying deliberately, is as he said; and whoever kills himself with something, Allah will punish him with it in the fire of Hell."
"1337","Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, my uncle Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Muslim, the guide of al-Amash, narrated to us, from Abu Abdillah, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no oath in disobedience to Allah, nor in what the son of Adam does not own; and whoever curses a Muslim is like killing him; and whoever calls a Muslim a disbeliever has disbelieved; and whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying deliberately, is as he said; and whoever kills himself with something by which he dies is in the Fire."
"1338","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Abdillah, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursing the believer is like killing him; and whoever declares a Muslim a disbeliever, one of them bears it. Abu al-Qasim said: This Abu Abdillah is said to be Khalid al-Hadhdha, and Khalid has two kunyas: Abu Munazil and Abu Abdillah."
"1339","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to me, Shuayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Awzai, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Abu Qilaba narrated to me, Thabit ibn al-Dahhak narrated to me, who said: A man vowed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to slaughter at Buwana. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have vowed to slaughter at Buwana. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Was there an idol of the idols of ignorance worshipped there? He said: No. He said: Was there a festival of their festivals there? He said: No. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fulfill your vow, for there is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, nor in severing kinship, nor in what the son of Adam does not own."
"1340","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Sulayman al-Shaybani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Saib narrated to us, who said: I asked Abdullah ibn Mughaffal about sharecropping (muzaraa), and he said: Thabit ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sharecropping."
"1341","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, both saying: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib, who said: I asked Abdullah ibn Mughaffal about sharecropping, and he said: Thabit ibn al-Dahhak narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sharecropping."
"1342","143 - Thabit ibn al-Samit al-Ansari. 1344 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habiba al-Ashhali narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Samit, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood praying in the mosque of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, wearing a cloak wrapped around him, placing his hand on it shielding it from the cold of the gravel."
"1343","144 - Thabit ibn Aqram al-Ansari, a Badri. 1345 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Thabit ibn Aqram ibn Thalaba ibn Adi ibn al-Ajlan."
"1344","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu al-Ajlan: Thabit ibn Aqram."
"1345","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition toward al-Ghamra in Najd, its commander Thabit ibn Aqram, and Thabit ibn Aqram was struck down in it."
"1346","145 - Thabit ibn al-Mundhir al-Ansari, a Badri. 1348 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu Adi ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar ibn Aws: Thabit ibn al-Mundhir ibn Haram ibn Amr ibn Zayd Manat ibn Adi ibn Amr."
"1347","146 - Thabit ibn Khalid ibn al-Numan ibn Khansa al-Ansari, a Badri, killed on the day of al-Yamama. 1349 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those Muslims killed on the day of al-Yamama, then of the Ansar, then of Banu Malik ibn Taymullah: Thabit ibn Khalid ibn al-Numan ibn Khansa."
"1348","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of al-Yamama, then from Banu al-Najjar: Thabit ibn Khalid ibn al-Numan."
"1349","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu al-Najjar: Thabit ibn Khalid ibn al-Numan ibn Khansa."
"1350","147 - Thabit ibn Atik al-Ansari, killed on the day of the bridge of al-Madain with Sad ibn Abi Waqqas in the year fifteen. 1352 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of the bridge of al-Madain with Sad ibn Abi Waqqas of the Ansar, then from Banu Amr ibn Mabdhul: Thabit ibn Atik."
"1351","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar killed on the day of the bridge: Thabit ibn Atik."
"1352","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of the bridge, then from Banu Amr ibn Mabdhul: Thabit ibn Atik."
"1353","148 - Thabit ibn Ajda al-Ansari, an Aqabi. 1355 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed al-Aqaba: Thabit ibn Ajda."
"1354","149 - Thabit ibn Thalaba al-Ansari, a Badri, martyred on the day of al-Taif. 1356 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu al-Khazraj, then from Banu Salima, then from Banu Haram: Thabit ibn Thalaba ibn Zayd ibn al-Harith ibn Haram."
"1355","Al-Hasan ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of al-Taif, then from Banu Salima: Thabit ibn Thalaba, and Thalaba who is called al-Jidh."
"1356","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of al-Taif: Thabit ibn al-Jidh."
"1357","150 - Thabit ibn Hazzal al-Ansari, a Badri. 1359 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj, then from Banu Balhubla: Thabit ibn Hazzal ibn Amr."
"1358","151 - Thabit ibn Rabia al-Ansari, a Badri. 1360 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj, then from Banu Balhubla: Thabit ibn Rabia."
"1359","152 - Thabit ibn Amr al-Ansari, a Badri. 1361 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu al-Najjar: Thabit ibn Amr ibn Zayd ibn Adi."
"1360","153 - Thabit ibn Hassan ibn Amr al-Ansari, a Badri. 1362 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu Adi ibn al-Najjar: Thabit ibn Hassan ibn Amr, he left no offspring."
"1361","154 - Thabit ibn Wadia al-Ansari, and it is said: Thabit ibn Yazid ibn Wadia ibn Khidham, and it is said: Thabit ibn Zayd, known as Abu Sad. 1363 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from Thabit ibn Wadia, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a lizard and said: A nation was transformed, and Allah knows best."
"1362","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from Thabit ibn Wadia, from the Prophet, the same."
"1363","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Thabit ibn Wadia, that a man of Banu Fazara brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lizards he had hunted, and he kept turning a lizard among them before him, and said: A nation was transformed, and to the best of my knowledge, he said: I do not know what happened to them, and I do not know, perhaps this is of them."
"1364","Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Yaman ibn Said al-Massisi narrated to us, Ashath ibn Shuba narrated to us, from Warqa ibn Umar, from Husayn, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Thabit ibn Zayd al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a roasted lizard; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a stick and began counting his fingers, then said: A nation of Banu Israil was transformed into beasts on the earth, and I do not know which beasts they are. He did not eat of it, nor did he forbid it."
"1365","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Husayn, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Thabit ibn Zayd al-Ansari, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people caught lizards and roasted them and ate them. I caught a lizard and roasted it, then brought it to the Prophet. He took a palm stalk and began counting his fingers with it, and said: A nation of Banu Israil was transformed into beasts on the earth, and I think perhaps it is this. I said: The people have roasted them and eaten them. He neither ate nor forbade."
"1366","155 - Thabit ibn al-Harith al-Ansari. 1368 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Thabit ibn al-Harith al-Ansari, who said: The Jews used to say: If a small boy of theirs perished, they said: He is a siddiq. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The Jews lied; there is no soul Allah creates in its mother's belly except that it is wretched or blessed. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, then revealed this verse: He knows you best when He produced you from the earth and when you were fetuses in your mothers' wombs, the whole verse."
"1367","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibn Lahia, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami, from Thabit ibn al-Harith al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted on the day of Khaybar to Sahla bint Asim ibn Adi and to a daughter of hers who was born."
"1368","156 - Thabit ibn Amr al-Ashjai, a Badri, an ally of the Ansar. 1370 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Thabit ibn Amr ibn Zayd ibn Adi ibn Sawwad ibn Usayma, an ally of them, from Ashja."
"1369","Chapter of those named Thalaba. 157 - Thalaba ibn al-Hakam al-Laythi. 1371 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, Simak ibn Harb informed us, from Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, who said: We captured sheep on the day of Khaybar, and the people plundered them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while their pots were boiling, and said: What is this? They said: Plunder, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Overturn them, for plunder is not lawful. So they overturned what remained in them."
"1370","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, all saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, brother of Banu Layth, informed me that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pass by pots containing sheep meat they had plundered, and he ordered them overturned, and said: Plunder is not lawful."
"1371","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plunder."
"1372","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida, and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, saying: My father informed me, from Simak ibn Harb, from Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, who said: We captured sheep on the day of Khaybar and plundered them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while their pots were boiling. They said: It is plunder. He said: Overturn the pots, for plunder is not lawful."
"1373","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi narrated to us, and al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, who said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) captured me while I was a youth, and I heard him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid plunder and order the pots overturned of domestic donkey meat."
"1374","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Affan ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Thalaba ibn al-Hakam say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: We do not eat plunder, for it is not lawful. I said to Simak: What is this plunder the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade? He said: Thalaba said: It is sheep they plundered on the day of Khaybar before distribution. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Overturn the pots."
"1375","Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Musa ibn Sufyan al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Simak ibn Harb, from Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Plunder is not lawful. Some people plundered sheep and informed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Overturn the pots and what is in them."
"1376","Ubayd ibn Ghannam informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, who said: We captured enemy sheep and plundered them and set our pots. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the pots and ordered them overturned, then said: Plunder is not lawful."
"1377","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abd al-Malik al-Juddi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Simak, from Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, who said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, and I heard him forbid plunder and order the pots overturned."
"1378","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sufyan, from Simak, from Thalaba, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"1379","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Maslama narrated to us, Ibrahim al-Talqani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Harb, from Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says to the scholars on the Day of Resurrection when He sits upon His throne to judge His servants: I did not place My knowledge and wisdom in you except that I want to forgive you for whatever was in you, and I do not care."
"1380","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Thalaba ibn al-Hakam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Plunder is not lawful."
"1381","158 - Thalaba Abu Abdillah al-Ansari. 1383 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Thalaba informed me, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab say: I heard your father Thalaba say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whichever man cuts off the right of a man by a false oath, it is a black spot of hypocrisy in his heart, nothing changes it until the Day of Resurrection."
"1382","159 - Thalaba ibn Zahdam al-Hanzali. 1384 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisa ibn Uqba narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Thalaba ibn Zahdam al-Hanzali, who said: A man of Banu Thalaba ibn Yarbu came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was preaching, saying: The giving hand is the upper; your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the nearest, the nearest. An Ansari man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, these Banu Thalaba ibn Yarbu struck so-and-so in ignorance. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exclaimed: No soul wrongs another."
"1383","160 - Thalaba Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari. 1385 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thalaba al-Ansari, from his father, that Amr ibn Habib ibn Abd Shams came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I stole a camel of Banu so-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to them, and they said: We have missed a camel of ours. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, and his hand was cut. Thalaba said: I look at him when his hand fell, saying: Praise be to Allah who purified me through you; you wanted to enter my body into the Fire."
"1384","161 - Thalaba ibn Abi Malik al-Qurazi. 1386 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Malik ibn Thalaba ibn Abi Malik, from his father, who said: A dispute was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the stream of Banu Qurayza, Mahzur. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged between them that the water is to the ankles, not withheld except to the lower."
"1385","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, freedman of Muzayna, narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Thalaba ibn Abi Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No harm, nor reciprocal harm. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in palm irrigation channels by the upper stream over the lower: the upper drinks, the water turns to the many, then the water is released to the lower, and likewise until the walls end and the water finishes."
"1386","162 - Thalaba ibn Saya. 1388 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, freedman of Zayd ibn Thabit, narrated to me, Said ibn Jubayr or Ikrima narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: When Abdullah ibn Salam, Thalaba ibn Saya, Asad ibn Ubayd, and those Jews who became Muslim, believed, testified, and desired Islam, the rabbis of the disbelieving Jews said: None believed in Muhammad nor followed him except our worst; had they been of our best they would not have left their fathers' religion. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed about their saying: They are not alike, of the People of the Book, to His saying: of the righteous."
"1387","163 - Thalaba ibn Suayr al-Udhri. 1389 - Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Wail, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Thalaba ibn Suayr, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood preaching and ordered sadaqat al-fitr upon the small, the large, the free, and the slave: a sa of dates, or a sa of barley, from each one, or from each head, and a sa of wheat between two."
"1388","Thalaba ibn Qayzi al-Ansari. 1390 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, in the hadith of Ibn Abi Rafi: Thalaba ibn Qayzi ibn Sakhr ibn Salama, a Badri."
"1389","165 - Thalaba ibn Hatib al-Ansari, a Badri. 1391 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, of al-Aws, then of Banu Amr ibn Awf, then of Banu Umayya ibn Zayd: Thalaba ibn Hatib."
"1390","166 - Thalaba ibn Saida, and it is said Ibn Sad al-Ansari, martyred on the day of Uhud. 1392 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of Uhud, then Banu Saida: Thalaba ibn Saida ibn Malik ibn Khalid ibn Thalaba ibn Haritha ibn Amr ibn al-Khazraj."
"1391","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of Uhud, then from Banu Saida: Thalaba ibn Sad ibn Malik."
"1392","167 - Thalaba ibn Amr al-Ansari, a Badri, killed on the day of the bridge of al-Madain in the year fifteen. 1394 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Thalaba ibn Mihsan ibn Amr ibn Ubayd."
"1393","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those killed on the day of the bridge of al-Madain with Sad ibn Abi Waqqas of the Ansar, then from Banu Amr ibn Mabdhul: Thalaba ibn Amr ibn Mihsan."
"1394","Al-Hasan ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those killed on the day of the bridge in the year fifteen: Thalaba ibn Amr ibn Mihsan."
"1395","168 - Thalaba al-Jidhai al-Ansari, a Badri. 1397 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu Jusham ibn al-Khazraj: Thalaba who is called al-Jidh."
"1396","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then of Banu al-Khazraj, then of Banu Salima, then of Banu Haram: Thalaba, who is called al-Jidh."
"1397","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of al-Taif, then from Banu Salim, then from Banu Haram: Thalaba who is called al-Jidh."
"1398","169 - Thalaba ibn Sad al-Saidi, brother of Sahl ibn Sad, a Badri. 1400 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Musab Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: My brother Thalaba ibn Sad witnessed Badr and was killed on the day of Uhud, and left no offspring."
"1399","170 - Thalaba ibn Anama al-Ansari, a Badri, an Aqabi, martyred on the day of al-Khandaq. 1401 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Thalaba ibn Anama ibn Adi."
"1400","Al-Hasan ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed al-Aqaba: Thalaba ibn Anama ibn Adi."
"1401","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of al-Khandaq, then from Banu Salima: Thalaba ibn Anama."
"1402","171 - Thumama al-Qurashi, and he is Thumama ibn Adi, and he witnessed Badr. 1404 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, that a Qurashi man called Thumama was over Sanaa; when Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, he preached and wept severely. When he recovered, he said: Today the caliphate of prophethood has been wrested from the nation of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and become kingship and tyranny; whoever takes something prevails over it."
"1403","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Anbari narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Abu Qahdham narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani, who said: There was a governor over Sanaa - Abu Qahdham said: called - Thumama ibn Adi - and he had companionship - and when the death notice of so-and-so came, he wept severely. When he recovered he said: This is when the caliphate of prophethood was wrested and became kingship and tyranny; whoever prevails over something owns it."
"1404","172 - Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among the rare musnad of Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, known as Abu Abdillah; it is said he is of Yemen, of Himyar, freedman of the family of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it is said captivity befell him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought him and freed him; he lived in Hims and died in the year fifty-four. 1406 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abi al-Sumayt narrated to us, from Qatada, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Madan ibn Abi Talha, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"1405","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Raqashi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Madan, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs while having what suffices him, blemish in his face on the Day of Resurrection."
"1406","And with his isnad he said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever leaves a treasure, it will be made for him on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent with two spots, following him, saying: I am your treasure you left after you. It will keep following him until it feeds him its hand, chewing it, then follows the rest of his body."
"1407","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to me, from Utba Abu Umayya al-Dimashqi, from Abu Sallam al-Aswad, from Thawban, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over the socks and the khimar, meaning the turban."
"1408","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Thawban, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he said: This journey is effort and hardship, so when one of you prays witr, let him pray two rakas; if he wakes, and otherwise they are for him."
"1409","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to me, from Abu al-Zahiriyya Hudayr ibn Kurayb, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Thawban, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered his sacrifice and said: Prepare some of it for us. We prepared it for him, and I kept feeding him from it until we arrived at Medina."
"1410","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every forgetfulness, two prostrations after the salam."
"1411","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Damdam ibn Zura, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Thawban, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, promised me of my nation seventy thousand not reckoned, with every thousand seventy thousand."
"1412","Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Tawba al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam say: Abu Asma narrated to me that Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a rabbi of the Jewish rabbis came and said: Peace be upon you, O Muhammad. I pushed him a push nearly knocking him down. He said: Why do you push me? I said: Why do you not say: O Messenger of Allah? The Jew said: We only call him by the name his family named him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My name is Muhammad, which my family named me. The Jew said: I came to ask you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Will it benefit you if I tell you? He said: I hear with my ears. He scratched with a stick he had and said: Ask. The Jew said: Where are the people on the day the earth is changed to other than the earth and the heavens? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are in the darkness below the bridge. He said: Who are the first people to cross? He said: The poor among the emigrants. The Jew said: What is their greeting when they enter Paradise? He said: The extra lobe of the fish liver. He said: What is their food after it? He said: The bull of Paradise which eats from its edges will be slaughtered for them. He said: What is their drink over it? He said: From a spring called Salsabil. He said: You spoke truthfully. I came to ask you about something none of the people of the earth knows except a prophet, or a man, or two men. He said: Will it benefit you if I tell you? He said: I hear with my ears. He said: I came to ask you about the child. He said: The man's fluid is white, and the woman's fluid is yellow; when they meet and the man's fluid prevails over the woman's fluid, male by Allah's permission; and when the woman's fluid prevails over the man's fluid, female by Allah's permission. The Jew said: You spoke truthfully, and you are a prophet. Then he left. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one asked me about what he asks me, and I had no knowledge of it until Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, informed me."
"1413","Talib ibn Qurra al-Udhuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said al-Asbahani narrated to us, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, all saying: Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu al-Khattab, from Abu Zura, from Abu Idris, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the briber, the bribed, and the intermediary."
"1414","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Abdillah al-Shami, from Aidhullah Abu Idris, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You do deeds unrecognized, and the bachelor is about to return to his family, joyful or grieved."
"1415","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man cupping in Ramadan while lending to a man, and said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"1416","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, saying: I heard Thawban say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold rings, silk brocade, saffron-dyed مقدم garments, and leopard skins."
"1417","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath informed us, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you visiting graves, so visit them, and make your visiting them prayer for them and seeking forgiveness for them; and I forbade you eating sacrificial meat after three, so eat of it and store; and I forbade you what is brewed in gourds, jars, and pitched vessels, so brew and benefit by them."
"1418","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Three with which no deed benefits: associating with Allah, disobedience to parents, and fleeing from battle."
"1419","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Compeller, the Exalted, will come on the Day of Resurrection and place His foot upon the bridge, saying: By My might and majesty, no wrongdoer shall pass Me. He will settle people against one another, until He settles the hornless sheep against the horn-broken by a butt it butted."
"1420","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cupped and gave the cupper his wage, and said: Feed the irrigation camel with it."
"1421","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, who said: Forty men of the companions gathered, discussing destiny and compulsion, among them Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them. The Trustworthy Spirit, Jibril, descended and said: O Muhammad, go out to your nation, for they have innovated. He went out to them at an hour he did not used to go out to them, and they disliked that from him. He went out to them with his color shining, his cheeks flushed, as if pomegranate seeds burst with sourness. They rose to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with bare forearms, their palms and forearms trembling, saying: We repent to Allah and His Messenger. He said: Woe to you, you almost incurred. The Trustworthy Spirit came to me and said: Go out to your nation, O Muhammad, for it has innovated."
"1422","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Banu al-Abbas have two banners, its top disbelief and its center misguidance; if you reach it, do not stray."
"1423","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah said: I saw Banu Marwan disputing my pulpit and it displeased me, and I saw Banu al-Abbas disputing my pulpit and it pleased me."
"1424","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with me and Banu al-Abbas; they divided my nation, shed its blood, and clothed it in black garments; Allah will clothe them in garments of Fire."
"1425","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When my companions are mentioned, withhold; and when the stars are mentioned, withhold; and when destiny is mentioned, withhold."
"1426","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, honor Islam by Umar ibn al-Khattab. He had struck his sister early in the night while she recited: Read in the name of your Lord who created, until I thought he killed her. Then he rose before dawn and heard her voice reciting: Read in the name of your Lord who created. He said: By Allah, this is neither poetry nor murmuring. He went until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found Bilal at the door and pushed the door. Bilal said: Who is this? He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: Until I seek permission for you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Bilal said: O Messenger of Allah, Umar is at the door. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If Allah wants good for Umar, He will admit him into the religion. He said to Bilal: Open. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his upper arms and shook him, saying: What do you want, and what have you come for? Umar said to him: Present to me what you call to. He said: Bear witness there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Umar became Muslim on the spot and said: Go out."
"1427","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The millstone of Islam is turning. He said: How shall we act, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Present my hadith against the Book; what agrees with it is from me, and I said it."
"1428","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah has overlooked for my nation three: error, forgetfulness, and what they were coerced upon."
"1429","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There will be peoples of my nation whose jurists deal in difficult questions; they are the worst of my nation."
"1430","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fosterage prohibits what lineage prohibits."
"1431","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu al-Aliya, from Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will guarantee me he will not ask people, and I guarantee him Paradise? Thawban said: I. Thawban would ask no one anything."
"1432","Ahmad ibn Masud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu al-Aliya, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"1433","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mina al-Ashjai, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Muawiya, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will guarantee me a trait and I guarantee him Paradise? I said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do not ask people anything. He said: Thawban's whip would fall while he was on his camel, and a man would go to hand it to him, so he would kneel his camel and take his whip."
"1434","Muhammad ibn Abda al-Massisi narrated to us, Abu Tawba al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Dawud, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a march and said: We are traveling by night, so no weak or difficult mount shall enter with us. A man mounted a difficult she-camel, which threw him; his thigh broke and he died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered prayer over him, then ordered Bilal, who called: Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient, three times."
"1435","Abu Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir Abd al-Ala ibn Mushir narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Abu Sallam al-Aswad, from Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My basin is between Aden and Amman; its water whiter than snow, sweeter than honey, and its most frequent comers the poor among the emigrants. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the poor among the emigrants? He said: Disheveled heads, dirty clothes, who do not marry luxurious women, nor are doors of سدad opened for them; who give the right upon them and are not given what is theirs."
"1436","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Ibn Khusayfa, from Ibn Adi, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three do not break the fast: cupping, vomiting, and wet dream; and the fasting person does not vomit deliberately."
"1437","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to me, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Abu Salama al-Kalai, who said: I heard Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a companion of his with a copper ring on his hand, and said: What is this? He said: Of wahina. He said: Remove it from you."
"1438","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu al-Judi, from Balj al-Mahri, from Abu Shayba al-Mahri, from Thawban, who said: We said: O Thawban, narrate to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomit and break the fast."
"1439","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Sad al-Baqqal, from Abu Salama, from Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution and says: I bear witness there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, entering from whichever he wills."
"1440","Abu Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Jad, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing repels decree except supplication; nothing increases lifespan except righteousness; and a man is deprived of provision by the sin he commits."
"1441","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My basin is between Aden and Amman; its cups as many as the stars, its water whiter than snow and sweeter than honey; the first to come to it the poor among the emigrants. We said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us. He said: Disheveled heads, dirty clothes, who do not marry منعm women, nor are doors of سدad opened for them; who give what is upon them and are not given what is theirs."
"1442","Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Thawban, from Hassan ibn Atiyya, from Abu Kabsha al-Saluli, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Be upright, and you will not encompass; know that among the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution except a believer."
"1443","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal informed us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ashath, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Thawban, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person remains in the harvest of Paradise. It was said: What is the harvest of Paradise? He said: Its fruits."
"1444","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person remains in the harvest of Paradise until he returns."
"1445","Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"1446","And from Thawban who said: The daughter of Hubayra came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a gold ring on her hand, and he mentioned the hadith."
"1447","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Rayhan ibn Said narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man is removed from Paradise, another returns in its place."
"1448","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, from Marzuq Abu Abdillah al-Shami, from Said al-Shami, who said: I heard Thawban say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is afflicted, for fever is a portion of the fire of Hell, let him extinguish it from him with cold water flowing, facing the flow of water, saying: O Allah, confirm Your Messenger, and heal Your servant, after dawn before sunrise, dipping in it three dips; if he is not cured in five, then in seven; if not cured in seven, then in nine; it hardly exceeds nine by Allah's permission."
"1449","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fasts Ramadan then follows it with six of Shawwal, that is fasting a year."
"1450","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from Marzuq Abu Abdillah al-Shami, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Thawban, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is imminent the nations gather against you, and he mentioned the hadith."
"1451","1453 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated to us, (ha) and Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Ma'mar al-Muq'ad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhada, Humayd al-Shami narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Munabbihi, from Thawban, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travelled, the last person of his household he parted from was Fatima, and when he returned the first one he entered upon was her. He said: He arrived from a campaign or a journey and found Fatima had hung a coarse cloth over her door and had put two silver bangles on al-Hasan and al-Husayn, so he turned back. She thought he turned back only because of what he saw, so she pulled down the curtain and removed the two bangles from the two boys and cut them up and pushed them to them. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping, so he said: O Thawban, take these two and go with them to a needy household in Madina, for these are my household and I dislike that they consume their good things in their worldly life. Then he said: O Thawban, buy for Fatima a necklace of sinew and two bracelets of ivory."
"1452","Thawban Abu Abd al-Rahman 1454 - Ahmad ibn al-Nasr al-Askari narrated to us, Isa ibn Hilal al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from his father, from his grandfather Thawban, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever you see reciting poetry in the mosque, say to him: May Allah smash your mouth, three times; and whomever you see announcing a lost item in the mosque, say to him: May you not find it, three times; and whomever you see buying and selling in the mosque, say to him: May Allah not profit your trade. Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us."
"1453","Thawra al-Sulami, kunya Abu Umama, grandfather of Man ibn Yazid 1455 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather, from Abu al-Juwayriya al-Jarmi, he said: I heard Man ibn Yazid say: I brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ruled in my favour, and he proposed marriage on my behalf and married me off, and I pledged allegiance to him, I and my grandfather."
"1454","Thaqif ibn Amr al-Asadi, ally of Banu Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf 1456 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, he said: There were killed on the day of Khaybar of Quraysh, then of Banu Abd Manaf: Thaqif ibn Amr, an ally of theirs from Banu Asad ibn Jazima."
"1455","Chapter of Jim. Jafar ibn Abi Talib, the one who flies in Paradise, may Allah be pleased with him, kunya Abu Abd Allah, his mother Fatima bint Asad ibn Hashim 1457 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Jafar to Muta in Jumada in the year eight."
"1456","1458 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubaydi narrated to us, Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar: That Jafar ibn Abi Talib wore his ring on his right hand."
"1457","1459 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced the deaths of the companions of Muta upon the pulpit, man by man, beginning with Zayd ibn Haritha, then Jafar ibn Abi Talib, then Abd Allah ibn Rawaha, may Allah have mercy on them. He said: Then Khalid ibn al-Walid took the banner, and he is a sword from the swords of Allah."
"1458","1460 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated to us, (ha) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced the death of Zayd and his two companions before the news reached him, while his eyes were shedding tears."
"1459","1461 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Yaqub, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army and appointed over them Zayd ibn Haritha: If he is killed and martyred then your commander is Jafar ibn Abi Talib, and if he is killed and martyred then your commander is Abd Allah ibn Rawaha. They set out and met the enemy. Zayd ibn Haritha took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Jafar ibn Abi Talib took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Abd Allah ibn Rawaha took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Khalid ibn al-Walid took the banner and Allah Almighty granted victory through him. Their news reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came out and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: As for what follows, your brothers met the enemy. Zayd ibn Haritha took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then Jafar took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then Abd Allah ibn Rawaha took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then a sword from the swords of Allah, Khalid ibn al-Walid, took the banner and Allah granted victory through him. Then he left the family of Jafar alone for three days before coming to them, then he came to them and said: Do not weep for him after today. Then he said: Call the sons of my brother to me. We were brought as though we were chicks, and he said: Call the barber to me. He ordered him and he shaved our heads. Then he said: As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib, and as for Awn, he resembles my appearance and character. Then he took my hand and lifted it and said: O Allah, succeed Jafar among his family, and bless Abd Allah in the deal of his right hand. He said it three times. He said: Our mother came and mentioned our orphanhood, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you fear poverty for them, while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter."
"1460","1462 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, my father who suckled me narrated to me, and he was one of Banu Murra ibn Awf, and he was in the campaign of Muta, he said: By Allah, it is as if I am looking at Jafar ibn Abi Talib when he hamstrung a blond horse of his, then fought the people until he was killed."
"1461","1463 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, al-Mughira ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed commanders in the campaign of Muta: Zayd ibn Haritha, and he said: If Zayd is killed then Jafar, and if Jafar is killed then Abd Allah ibn Rawaha. Abd Allah said: I was with them in that campaign, and we searched for Jafar and found on the front of his body more than ninety wounds, between stabs and shots."
"1462","1464 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Karim al-Zafaran al-Askari narrated to us, Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban al-Warraq narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We missed Jafar ibn Abi Talib and searched for him and found him among the slain, and found on him more than ninety wounds, between sword cuts, spear stabs and arrow shots, and we found that on the front of him."
"1463","1465 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Nafi, freedman of Ibn Umar, that Abd Allah ibn Umar informed him that he stood over Jafar on that day while he was slain. He said: I counted in him fifty wounds, between stabs and cuts, with none of them in his back."
"1464","1466 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Zamaa ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salama ibn Wahram, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise last night and looked in it, and there was Jafar flying with the angels."
"1465","1467 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jabara ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, Abu Shayba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Jafar ibn Abi Talib as an angel flying in Paradise, with two wings with which he flies wherever he wishes, his forefeathers clipped short and stained with blood."
"1466","1468 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, my uncle Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Qutba ibn Abd al-Aziz, from al-Amash, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shown them in sleep, and he saw Jafar as an angel with two wings stained with blood, and Zayd facing him upon a couch."
"1467","1469 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, my uncle Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Shabi, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, it was said to him: Jafar has arrived from the Negus, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not know with which of the two I am more joyful, the arrival of Jafar or the conquest of Khaybar. And he kissed between his eyes."
"1468","1470 - Ahmad ibn Khalid ibn Musarrih al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Musarrih Abu Wahb narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, he said: When Jafar arrived from the migration to Abyssinia, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him and embraced him and kissed between his eyes and said: I do not know with which of the two I am more delighted, the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Jafar."
"1469","1471 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, she said: When the death of Jafar reached us, we recognized grief in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1470","1472 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Khalid, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: When the news of Jafar came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prepare food for the family of Jafar, for there has come to them what occupies them."
"1471","1473 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Qutba ibn Abd al-Aziz, from al-Amash, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shown in sleep the companions of Muta, and he saw Jafar as an angel with two wings stained with blood, meaning dyed."
"1472","1474 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Amir al-Shabi, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that when he greeted Abd Allah ibn Jafar he would say: Peace be upon you, O son of the one with two wings."
"1473","1475 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida, from al-Shabi: That Jafar ibn Abi Talib was killed on the day of Muta in al-Balqa."
"1474","1476 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: I would ask Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, for something and he would refuse me, so I would say: By the right of Jafar. And when I said, By the right of Jafar, he would give me."
"1475","1477 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Asad al-Kindi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated to us, Abu Ishaq Ibrahim al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Jafar loved the poor; he would sit with them, narrating to them and they narrating to him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to call him the father of the poor."
"1476","What Jafar narrated, may Allah be pleased with him 1478 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Adam al-Massisi narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, both said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, both said: Asad ibn Amr al-Kufi narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, he said: Quraysh sent Amr ibn al-As and Umara ibn al-Walid with a gift from Abu Sufyan to the Negus, and they said to him while we were with him: Some low and foolish people of ours have been sent to you, so hand them over to us. He said: No, until I hear their speech. So he sent for us and said: What do you say? We said: Our people worship idols, and Allah Almighty sent a Messenger to us, so we believed in him and affirmed him. The Negus said to them: Are they slaves of yours? They said: No. He said: Do you have a debt over them? They said: No. He said: Then leave them alone. We left him, then Amr ibn al-As said: These people say about Jesus other than what you say. He said: If they do not say about Jesus as I say, I will not leave them in my land for an hour of daytime. He sent for us, and the second summons was harder on us than the first. He said: What does your companion say about Jesus son of Mary? We said: He says: He is the Spirit of Allah and His Word which He cast to the chaste virgin. He sent and said: Call so-and-so the priest and so-and-so the monk. Some of them came to him and he said: What do you say about Jesus son of Mary? They said: You know best, what do you say? The Negus took something from the ground then said: Jesus is like this; he did not exceed what these people said by even this much. Then he said to them: Does anyone harm you? They said: Yes. So he ordered a crier who announced: Whoever harms any of them, fine him four dirhams. Then he said: Is that enough for you? We said: No, so he doubled it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) migrated to Madina and prevailed there, we said to him: Our companion has gone out to Madina and prevailed there and migrated, and killed those about whom we told you, and we wish to depart to him, so provision us. He said: Yes. So he carried us and provisioned us and gave us, then said: Inform your companion of what I did for you, and this messenger of mine is with you, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that he is the Messenger of Allah, so tell him to seek forgiveness for me. Jafar said: We left until we came to Madina. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me and embraced me and said: I do not know whether I rejoice more at the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Jafar. Then he sat, and the messenger of the Negus stood and said: Here is Jafar, so ask him what our companion did with him. I said: Yes, he did such-and-such with us, and carried us and provisioned us and aided us, and bore witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah, and said: Tell him to seek forgiveness for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and performed ablution then supplicated three times: O Allah, forgive the Negus. The Muslims said: Amen. Jafar said: I said to the messenger: Go and inform your master of what you saw of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the wording is that of the hadith of Muhammad ibn Adam."
"1477","1479 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai narrated to us, (ha) and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir narrated to us, both from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Umm Salama, from Jafar ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Negus asked him: What is your religion? He said: There has been sent among us a Messenger whose language, truthfulness and fidelity we know. He called us to worship Allah alone, associating nothing with Him, and to abandon what our people and others used to worship besides Him. He commands us to good and forbids us evil, and commanded us with prayer, fasting, charity and joining kinship. He called us to what we recognize, and recited to us a revelation that came from Allah, like which nothing else is. So we affirmed him and believed in him, and knew that what he brought is truth from Allah. At that our people parted from us, harmed us and overpowered us. When they did to us what we dislike and we could not defend ourselves against them, we came out to your land and chose you over others. The Negus said: Go, you are safe in my land; whoever insults you shall pay a fine."
"1478","Sulayman ibn Surad from Jubayr ibn Mutim 1480 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad al-Khuzai, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: Ritual washing from major impurity was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: As for me, I pour over my head three times. Then he gestured with his hand as though pouring with them over the head."
"1479","1481 - Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi and Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Bukayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: Washing from major impurity was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: As for me, I pour over my head three times."
"1480","1482 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, (ha) and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Yahya al-Ushnani narrated to us, both said: Zaida narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: We discussed washing from major impurity in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I pour over my head handfuls of water, and I wash my head from major impurity."
"1481","1483 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, both said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: We discussed washing from major impurity in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man among us said: How should we do? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I take a handful and pour over my head, then afterwards pour over the rest of my body."
"1482","1484 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, (ha) and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (ha) and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, all said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Surad al-Khuzai narrated to me, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, that they mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washing from major impurity, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I pour over my head three times, and he gestured with both his hands."
"1483","1485 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ammar ibn Matar narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: We disputed about washing in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I pour over my head three handfuls."
"1484","1486 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both said: Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: They disputed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about washing from major impurity, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I pour over my head three times."
"1485","1487 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi and Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, both said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: Washing was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: As for me, it suffices me to pour over my head three times a handful for major impurity."
"1486","1488 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: We mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washing from major impurity, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I perform ablution as for prayer, then I take a handful three times and pour it over my head, then I wash."
"1487","1489 - Ahmad ibn al-Khadir al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abda al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu Muadh al-Nahwi al-Fadl ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abu Hamza al-Sukkari narrated to us, from Raqaba ibn Masqala, from Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Hamdani, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: Washing from major impurity was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: As for me, I pour over my head three times."
"1488","Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar from Jubayr ibn Mutim 1490 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, both said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Talha ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A Qurashi has the strength of two men of other than Quraysh. A questioner asked Ibn Shihab: What does he mean by that? He said: Soundness of judgment."
"1489","Chapter of Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from his father 1491 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite al-Tur in Maghrib."
"1490","1492 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite al-Tur in Maghrib."
"1491","1493 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the ransom of the people of Badr, and I heard him recite in Maghrib: By the Mount, and a Book inscribed."
"1492","1494 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (ha) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qanabi and Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, (ha) and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, (ha) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, all said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrate from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite al-Tur in Maghrib. And the wording is that of al-Humaydi."
"1493","1495 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Qust al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite al-Tur in Maghrib."
"1494","1496 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Yunus and Nafi ibn Yazid, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite al-Tur in Maghrib."
"1495","1497 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Qurra and Uqayl and Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Maghrib: By the Mount and a Book inscribed."
"1496","1498 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd informed me that Ibn Shihab informed him, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that he came regarding the ransom of the captives of the people of Badr. He said: I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in the Maghrib prayer: By the Mount, and a Book inscribed, in parchment unrolled. He said: His recitation seized me as with distress, and that was the first I heard of the matter of Islam."
"1497","1499 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayda narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri - Hushaym said: I do not think but that I heard it from al-Zuhri - from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to speak to him about the captives of Badr, and I found him praying Maghrib or Isha with his companions, and I heard him saying or reciting, his voice having come out of the mosque: Indeed the punishment of your Lord will occur; of it there is no preventer. It was as though my heart cracked."
"1498","1500 - Abdan ibn Ahmad al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, Burd ibn Sinan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite al-Tur in Maghrib."
"1499","1501 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite al-Tur in Maghrib."
"1500","1502 - Yaqub ibn Ghaylan al-Umani narrated to us, Urwa ibn Said al-Rabai al-Misri narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying Isha or Maghrib with his companions, and I heard him reciting, his voice having come out of the mosque: Indeed the punishment of your Lord will occur; of it there is no preventer. It was as though it split from my heart."
"1501","1503 - Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn al-Hajjaj al-Zubaydi narrated to us, Abu Huma narrated to us, Abu Qurra narrated to us, he said: Zamaa ibn Salih mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the captives of Badr, and he prayed Maghrib with the people and recited in it al-Tur."
"1502","1504 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the captives of Badr: Had al-Mutim ibn Adi been alive and spoken to me about these foul ones, I would have left them for him."
"1503","1505 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (ha) and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, both said: Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had Mutim ibn Adi been alive then spoken to me about these foul ones, or about these captives, I would have released them, meaning the captives of Badr."
"1504","1506 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayd narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to speak to him about the captives of Badr, so he said: Had he come to us regarding them, we would have granted him intercession, meaning his father al-Mutim ibn Adi. Hushaym said: He had a favour with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1505","1507 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he come to me regarding these foul ones, I would have granted him intercession, meaning al-Mutim ibn Adi. At that Jubayr accepted Islam."
"1506","1508 - Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Zubaydi narrated to us, Abu Huma Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Qurra narrated to us, he said: Zamaa ibn Salih mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the ransom of the people of Badr, and when I spoke to him he said: Had Mutim ibn Adi been with me then spoken to me about these, I would have released them for him. And Mutim ibn Adi had a favour with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1507","Chapter 1509 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No severer shall enter Paradise."
"1508","1510 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me that Jubayr ibn Mutim informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No severer shall enter Paradise."
"1509","1511 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (ha) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both said: Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim narrated to me, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No severer shall enter Paradise. Sufyan said: Its explanation is severer of kinship ties. And the wording is that of al-Humaydi."
"1510","1512 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No severer shall enter Paradise."
"1511","1513 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, (ha) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, both said: Ismail ibn Ulayya narrated to us, all from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No severer shall enter Paradise."
"1512","1514 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, (ha) and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, both said: al-Zubaydi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No severer shall enter Paradise. Baqiyya added in his hadith: of kinship."
"1513","1515 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn and Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No severer shall enter Paradise."
"1514","1516 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Numayr al-Sadafi al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Qurra ibn Abd al-Rahman and Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No severer shall enter Paradise."
"1515","1517 - Abu Zura al-Dimashqi and Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamza informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No severer shall enter Paradise."
"1516","1518 - Abu Khalifa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Juwayriya narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, that Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed him that his father informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No severer shall enter Paradise."
"1517","1519 - al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi narrated to us, Ali ibn Ziyad al-Lahji narrated to us, Abu Qurra narrated to us, he said: Zamaa ibn Salih mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No severer shall enter Paradise."
"1518","Chapter 1520 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I have names. I am Ahmad, and I am Muhammad, and I am al-Mahi by whom unbelief is effaced, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet people shall be gathered, and I am al-Aqib. He said: I said to al-Zuhri: What is al-Aqib? He said: The one after whom there is no Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1519","1521 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir al-Bakhtari al-Tai narrated to us, Bishr ibn Shuayb ibn Abi Hamza narrated to us, from his father, from al-Zuhri, Muhammad ibn Jubayr informed me, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I have five names. I am Ahmad, and I am Muhammad, and I am al-Mahi by whom Allah effaces unbelief, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet people shall be gathered, and I am al-Aqib."
"1520","1522 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qanabi and Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, (ha) and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, all said: Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have names. I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom unbelief is effaced, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet people shall be gathered, and I am al-Aqib after whom there is no Prophet."
"1521","1523 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: I have names. I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom Allah effaces unbelief, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet people shall be gathered, and I am al-Aqib after whom there is no Prophet."
"1522","1524 - Yusuf al-Qadi and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: I have names. I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom I efface unbelief, and I am al-Hashir by whom I gather people at my feet, and I am al-Aqib after whom there is no Prophet."
"1523","1525 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have names. I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom unbelief is effaced, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet people shall be gathered, and I am al-Aqib, and al-Aqib is the one after whom there is no one. And Allah has named him compassionate, merciful."
"1524","1526 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, both said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have names. I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and al-Mahi by whom Allah effaces unbelief, and al-Hashir at whose feet people shall be gathered, and al-Aqib. I asked Sufyan: What is al-Aqib? He said: The last of the Prophets."
"1525","1527 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamza informed us, from al-Zuhri, Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I have names. I am Muhammad and Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom Allah effaces the unbelievers, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet people shall be gathered, and I am al-Aqib."
"1526","1528 - Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have names. I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom Allah effaces the unbelievers, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet people shall be gathered, and I am al-Aqib."
"1527","1529 - al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Tayyib al-Sanani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have five names. I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom Allah effaces unbelief, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet people shall be gathered, and I am al-Aqib."
"1528","1530 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: I read to Abd Allah ibn Nafi, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"1529","1531 - Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abada al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran, from Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: al-Mutim ibn Adi said: You have done to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what you have done, so be the most restrained of people from him. Abu Jahl ibn Hisham said: Rather be the severest as you were. Al-Harith ibn Amir ibn Nawfal said: By Allah, the affair of Muhammad will ever remain ascendant whether you oppose him openly or secretly. Abu Yusuf said: al-Harith was killed on the day of Badr as a disbeliever."
"1530","1532 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Misri al-Tahhan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: I found in a book in Madina, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi, and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: Abu Jahl ibn Hisham said when he arrived in Makka returning from Hamza: O company of Quraysh, Muhammad has settled in Yathrib and sent his scouts, and he only wishes to strike at you. Beware of passing his road or approaching him, for he is like a ferocious lion. He is enraged at you; you expelled him as ticks are expelled from camel hoofs. By Allah, he has sorcerers; I never saw him nor any of his companions but I saw devils with them. You know the enmity of the two sons of Qayla, so he is an enemy aided by an enemy. Mutim ibn Adi said to him: O Abu al-Hakam, by Allah I never saw anyone truer of tongue nor truer of promise than your brother whom you drove away. Since you have done what you did, be the most restrained of people from him. Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith said: Be the severest as you were, for if the two sons of Qayla prevail over you they will show you neither kinship nor covenant. If you obey me you will feed them the news of Kinana, or they will expel Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from among them so he becomes solitary and driven away. As for the two sons of Qayla, by Allah they and the people of your lowland in humiliation are but equal, and I shall spare you their edge. He said: That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I shall surely kill them and crucify them and guide them though they hate it. I am a mercy; Allah Almighty sent me, and He will not take me until Allah manifests His religion. I have five names. I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom Allah effaces unbelief, and I am al-Hashir at whose hands people shall be gathered, and I am al-Aqib. Ahmad ibn Salih said: I hope the hadith is sound."
"1531","1533 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Mansur al-Kisai narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say to his companions: Come with us to Banu Waqif, let us visit the sightless one. Sufyan said: A clan of the Ansar, and the sightless one was blind."
"1532","1534 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Jammal al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say to his companions: Come with us to Banu Waqif, let us visit the sightless one. Sufyan said: A clan of the Ansar, and he was veiled of sight."
"1533","1535 - Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Amiri al-Kufi narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not have the call made for him in any travel prayer except the iqama, except Fajr, for he would have both the adhan and iqama made."
"1534","1536 - Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Umar ibn Hisham Abu Umayya al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of Attab ibn Bashir, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father Jubayr, he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Uthman ibn Talha when he handed him the key of the Kaaba: Here, hide it. He said: Hence the key is hidden."
"1535","1537 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Idris ibn Umar, secretary of al-Humaydi, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ibrahim, of the descendants of Jubayr ibn Mutim, narrated to us, Umm Uthman bint Said, my grandmother, narrated to me, from her father Said ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: I went out trading to Sham in the pre-Islamic period, and when I was at the nearest part of Sham a man of the People of the Book met me and said: Is there among you a man who has claimed prophethood? I said: Yes. He said: Would you recognize his image if you saw it? I said: Yes. He took me into a house with images, but I did not see the image of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While I was thus, a man of theirs entered upon us and said: What are you about? We told him, so he took us to his house. As soon as I entered I looked at the image of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was a man holding the heel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Who is this man standing at his heel? He said: There was no Prophet but there was a Prophet after him except this one, for there is no Prophet after him, and this is the successor after him. And there was the description of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1536","1538 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn Rishdin narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: Qurra ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Haywil informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say, My soul has become wicked, but let him say, My soul has become heavy."
"1537","1539 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Ubada al-Zuraqi narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Juhfa, and he came out to us and said: Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and that the Quran has come from Allah? We said: Yes. He said: Then rejoice, for this Quran, one end is in the Hand of Allah and one end is in your hands. Hold fast to it and you will never perish after it."
"1538","1540 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Manda al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I and so-and-so walked to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave Banu al-Muttalib and left us, though we and they are to you of one standing. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib are one thing."
"1539","1541 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt Abu Yala al-Tawwazi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus and Abda narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say at the Khayf of Mina: May Allah brighten a servant who heard my words and memorized and understood them and conveyed them to one who did not hear them. Many a carrier of understanding has no understanding, and many a carrier of understanding conveys to one more understanding than him. Three things the heart of a believer does not deceive over: sincerity of deed for Allah, good counsel to the rulers of the Muslims, and holding to their community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."
"1540","1542 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, my uncle Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Salam, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the Khayf of Mina and mentioned the like of it."
"1541","1543 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Khayf of Mina say: May Allah brighten a servant who heard my words and memorized them then conveyed them to one who did not hear them. Many a carrier of understanding has no understanding, and many a carrier of understanding conveys to one more understanding than him. Three things the heart of a believer does not deceive over: sincerity of deed for Allah, obedience to those in authority, and holding to the community, for their supplication is behind them."
"1542","1544 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the Khayf and said: May Allah brighten a servant who heard my words and understood them and conveyed them to one who did not hear them. Many a carrier of understanding has no understanding, and many a carrier of understanding conveys to one more understanding than him. Three things the heart of a believer does not deceive over: sincerity of deed for Allah, obedience to those in authority, and holding to the community of the Muslims, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."
"1543","1545 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father Jubayr ibn Mutim, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which land is worst? He said: I do not know. When Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon them both, he said: Which land is worst? He said: I do not know until I ask my Lord. Jibril, peace be upon him, departed and remained as long as Allah willed, then said: O Muhammad, you asked me which land is worst, and I said, I do not know. I asked my Lord and said: Which land is worst? He said: Its markets."
"1544","1546 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfa narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"1545","1547 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, (ha) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, all said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrate from Yaqub ibn Utba, from Jubayr ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, souls are strained, dependents are lost, wealth has perished and livestock are emaciated, so ask Allah Almighty for rain for us. We seek intercession by you to Allah, and seek intercession by Allah to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, do you know what you say? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) glorified Allah and kept glorifying until that was seen in the faces of his companions. Then he said: Woe to you, Allah is not interceded by to any of His creation; the affair of Allah is greater than that. Woe to you, do you know what Allah Almighty is? His Throne is over His heavens and His earth like this, and he gestured with his two fingers, like a dome. And it creaks with Him like the creaking of a saddle with a rider."
"1546","1548 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty tests His servant with illness until He expiates from him every sin."
"1547","1549 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the road to Makka. He said: The people of Yemen have come to you like clouds, the best of those on earth. A man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, except us? He fell silent, then he repeated it and he fell silent, then he repeated it, so he said in a low word: Except you."
"1548","1550 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami, from al-Harith ibn Abi Dhib, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head to the sky and said: The people of Yemen have come to you like pieces of the dark night, and they are the best people of the earth. A man among those with him said: And of us, O Messenger of Allah? He said in a low word: Except you."
"1549","Chapter 1551 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, that his father informed him that: While he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the people on their return from Hunayn, the Bedouins clung to him asking him and forced him to a samura tree which snatched his cloak while he was on his mount. He stopped and said: Return my cloak to me. Do you fear miserliness from me? By Allah, if livestock equal in number to these thorn trees were mine I would divide them among you, then you would not find me miserly nor cowardly nor lying."
"1550","1552 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, that Muhammad ibn Jubayr said: Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me that while he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the people on their return from Hunayn, the Bedouins clung to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him until they forced him to a samura tree which snatched his cloak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped and said: Give me my cloak. Had I livestock equal in number to these thorn trees I would divide them among you, then you would not find me miserly nor lying nor cowardly."
"1551","1553 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Anbasa ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me, that Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim said: Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me that while he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his return from Hunayn, the Bedouins clung to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him until they forced him by a lote tree which snatched the cloak of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He stopped and said: For Allah's sake, give me my cloak. Had livestock equal in number to these thorn trees been mine I would have divided them among you, and you would not find me miserly nor cowardly nor lying."
"1552","1554 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me, that Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim said: Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me that while he was traveling with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the people on their return from Hunayn, the Bedouins clung to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him until they forced him to a samura tree which snatched his cloak. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped and said: Give me my cloak. Had I livestock equal in number to these thorn trees I would divide them, then you would not find me miserly nor lying nor cowardly."
"1553","1555 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamza narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me, that Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim said: Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me that while he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the people on their return from Hunayn, the Bedouins clung to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him until they forced him to a samura tree which snatched his cloak. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped and said: Give me my cloak. Had livestock equal in number to these thorn trees been mine I would divide them among you, then you would not find me miserly nor untruthful nor cowardly."
"1554","1556 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (ha) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Azraq narrated to us, (ha) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, all said: Sufyan narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me, from his father, he said: I lost a camel of mine on the day of Arafat and went out seeking it at Arafat, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing with the people at Arafat. I said: This is of the Hums, so what is he doing here? Sufyan said: al-Ahmas is one strict in his religion. Quraysh were called the Hums, and Satan had lured them and said to them: If you revere other than your sanctuary, people will deem your sanctuary light. And they would not leave the Sanctuary."
"1555","1557 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke to him about something, so he ordered her to return to him. She said: O Messenger of Allah, if I come and do not find you, meaning death. He said: If you do not find me, then go to Abu Bakr."
"1556","1558 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"1557","1559 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The moon split in the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1558","1560 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Masud al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah al-Dashtaki informed us, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jubayr ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: The moon split while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1559","1561 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mundhir al-Tariqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: The moon split while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1560","Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from his father 1562 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Ghurab al-Kufi narrated to us, (ha) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other than it except the Sacred Mosque."
"1561","1563 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyya, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Hashir, and al-Mahi, and al-Khatam, and al-Aqib."
"1562","1564 - Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid al-Himsi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father Jubayr, that he heard him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Aqib, and al-Hashir, and al-Mahi."
"1563","1565 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Ibn Aisha narrated to us, (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, all said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey of his and said: Who will guard us tonight lest we sleep past the Fajr prayer? Bilal said: I. He faced the sunrise, and their ears were struck until the heat of the sun woke them. Then they stood and led their mounts, then performed ablution, and Bilal called the adhan, then they prayed the two rak'as of Fajr, then prayed Fajr."
"1564","1566 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (ha) and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and Abu Khalifa and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, all said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty descends every night to the lowest heaven and says: Is there an asker that I may give him? Is there a seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him?"
"1565","1567 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Abd Manaf, if you are given this authority one day, do not prevent a circumambulator circumambulating this House at any hour of night or day."
"1566","1568 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Asim, from a man of Anaza, from Ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enter into prayer and say: Allah is Most Great, greatly, three times, and praise be to Allah abundantly, three times. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his blowing, his breathing and his prodding. Amr said: His blowing is pride, his prodding is madness, and his breathing is poetry."
"1567","1569 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki and Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Misar, from Amr ibn Murra, from a man of Anaza, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he entered into prayer and said: Allah is Most Great, greatly, three times, and praise be to Allah abundantly, three times, and glory be to Allah morning and evening, three times. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his prodding, his blowing and his breathing."
"1568","1570 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Husayn, from Amr ibn Murra, he said: Ammar ibn Asim narrated to me, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opened the prayer he would say: Allah is Most Great, greatly, three times, and praise be to Allah abundantly, three times, and glory be to Allah morning and evening, three times. Then he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan, from his prodding, his breathing and his blowing. And he would say: His breathing is poetry, his blowing is pride, and his prodding is that which dies in its affliction."
"1569","1571 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, (ha) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Husayn, from Amr ibn Murra, Ammar ibn Asim narrated to me, Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim narrated to me, from his father: That he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha."
"1570","1572 - Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say in his bowing: Glory be to my Lord the Almighty, and in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord the Most High."
"1571","1573 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Firdaws ibn al-Ashari narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Walking on foot to the Friday prayers are expiations for sins, perfecting ablution in cold hardships, and awaiting prayer after prayers."
"1572","1574 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Thabit ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a share among some people, and the people followed him and he passed by a tree which caught his clothes. He said: Return my clothes to me. Do you fear for me? By Allah, had I wealth I would have divided it."
"1573","1575 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Manda narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Firdaws ibn al-Ashari narrated to us, from Masud ibn Sulayman, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said while at the pass of al-Araka, giving when he had finished from Hunayn. He turned to us with his face like a piece of the moon."
"1574","1576 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Manda al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Adi narrated to us, from Hatim ibn Ismail, from al-Juayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sister's son of a people is of them."
"1575","1577 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm - narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing upon a camel of his at Arafat apart from his people until he departed after them, by a grant from Allah to him."
"1576","1578 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar ibn al-Naqid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from his uncle Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: Quraysh would only depart from Muzdalifa, saying: We are the Hums, so we do not leave the Sanctuary. They abandoned the stand at Arafat. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing with the people at Arafat upon a camel of his, departing with them, until he came in the morning with his people to Muzdalifa and halted with them, then departed when they departed."
"1577","1579 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have grown heavy, so do not race me in standing in prayer, bowing and prostration."
"1578","1580 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Salim al-Saigh narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance there was in the pre-Islamic period, Islam only increased it in strength."
"1579","1581 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri narrated to us, Abda ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Manda al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from his father, from Mansur, from Kilab ibn Ali al-Wahidi, of Banu Amir, from Ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon al-Marwa in his umra shortening his hair, saying: Umra has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. No celibacy."
"1580","1582 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Manda narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muslim ibn Qutayba narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Mudrik ibn Ali, from Mansur ibn Abi Sulayman, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shorten upon al-Marwa with shears, and he said: Umra has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"1581","1583 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruwasi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of Arafat is a standing place, but keep away from Urana. All of Muzdalifa is a standing place, but keep away from the valley of Muhassir. All the days of Tashriq are slaughter, and all the passes of Makka are a sacrifice place."
"1582","1584 - Muhammad ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ibn Dab narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Muhammad ibn Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visit Said ibn al-As, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) foment him with a cloth."
"1583","1585 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari and Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Rajai narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Abu Amr al-Sadusi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman informed me, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: I arrived in Madina when I arrived, and I was not a Muslim that day. I arrived overcome by intense drowsiness, so I slept in the mosque until I was startled by the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting: By the Mount, and a Book inscribed. I said: To Allah we return, until I left the mosque. And that was the first Islam entered my heart."
"1584","1586 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, glory be to You O Allah and with Your praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You, and says it in a gathering of remembrance, it is like a seal stamped upon it. Whoever says it in a gathering of idle talk, it is an expiation for him."
"1585","1587 - Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani, (ha) and Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, both said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The expiation of a gathering is that one not rise until he says: Glory be to You O Allah and with Your praise, there is no god but You, turn to me and forgive me. He says it three times. If it was a gathering of clamour it is an expiation for him, and if it was a gathering of remembrance it is a stamp upon it."
"1586","1588 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ayyub al-Sarifini narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays toward a sutra, let him draw near to it, lest Satan pass between him and it."
"1587","1589 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Isa ibn Hilal al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Jabala, from Abu al-Hasan, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Swords are not to be unsheathed, nor arrows scattered, in the mosques. No oath by Allah is to be sworn in the mosque. The midday rest in the mosques is not to be denied, neither to a resident nor a guest. They are not to be built with images nor adorned with bottles, for they were built with trust and honoured with dignity."
"1588","1590 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzar al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prescribed punishments are not to be carried out in the mosques."
"1589","Said ibn al-Musayyab from Jubayr ibn Mutim, may Allah be pleased with him 1591 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote the share of the near kin, of Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib, I and Uthman ibn Affan came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, these are Banu Hashim; their merit is not denied because of your place whom Allah placed among them. Tell us: You gave our brothers of Banu al-Muttalib and withheld from us, though we and they are to you of one standing? He said: They did not part from me in pre-Islamic times nor in Islam. Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib are one thing. And he interlaced his fingers."
"1590","1592 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"1591","1593 - Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, Said ibn al-Musayyab informed me that Jubayr ibn Mutim informed him that he and Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speaking to him about what he divided of the fifth of Khaybar between Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you divided for our brothers Banu al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf and gave us nothing, though our kinship is like their kinship. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: I see Hashim and al-Muttalib as one thing. Jubayr ibn Mutim said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not divide for Banu Abd Shams nor for Banu Nawfal of that fifth anything, as he divided for Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib."
"1592","1594 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, that Uthman ibn Affan asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he gave Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib of the fifth of Khaybar and did not give Banu Abd Shams nor Banu Abd Manaf. He said: Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib are one thing."
"1593","Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from Jubayr ibn Mutim 1595 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, one of my brothers narrated to me, from my father, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, that he came to Madina for a ransom while he was then a polytheist. He entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying Maghrib, and he recited al-Tur. It was as though my heart cracked at the recitation of the Quran."
"1594","1596 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying Maghrib, and it was as though my heart split, or cracked, when I heard the Quran."
"1595","1597 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr and Abd Allah ibn Numayr and Abu Usama narrated to us, all from Zakariya, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance there was in the pre-Islamic period, Islam only increased it in strength."
"1596","Abd al-Aziz ibn Jurayj from Jubayr ibn Mut'im. 1598 - Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: my father informed me, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: I lost a donkey on the day of Arafah, so I went out seeking it, and behold the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing on his camel, and that was after revelation had been sent down to him."
"1597","Abdullah ibn Babayh from Jubayr ibn Mut'im. 1599 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Abdullah ibn Babayh reporting from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O sons of Abd Manaf, O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, I shall surely know you to have prevented no person from praying at this House at whatever hour he wishes, by night or day."
"1598","1600 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Abdullah ibn Babah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib and O sons of Abd Manaf, if you are given charge of any of this affair, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House from praying at any hour of night or day."
"1599","1601 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Abu al-Zubayr narrated to him, from Ibn Babayh, that he heard Jubayr ibn Mut'im saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O sons of Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House at any hour of night or day."
"1600","1602 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Babayh, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I shall surely know you, O sons of Abd Manaf, to have prevented no circumambulator circling this House at an hour of night or day."
"1601","Mujahid ibn Jabr from Jubayr ibn Mut'im. 1603 - Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Qurrah, nephew of al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar, narrated to us, Raja, the keeper of al-Rakiyy, narrated to us, from Mujahid Abu al-Hajjaj, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd Manaf, O sons of Abd al-Dar, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House and prays at any hour of night or day."
"1602","Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah from Jubayr ibn Mut'im. 1604 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Muhammad ibn Rukanah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"1603","1605 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"1604","1606 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Husayn, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah al-Muttalibi, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"1605","1607 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Husayn, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in my mosque exceeds other mosques by a thousand prayers except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"1606","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, may Allah be pleased with him. 1608 - Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Ata, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: I was with Quraysh in their dwelling short of Arafah, and I lost a donkey, so I went out seeking it among the people at Arafah, and I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafah."
"1607","Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi from Jubayr ibn Mut'im. 1609 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amir ibn Yahya, from Ulayy ibn Rabah, who narrated to him, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: I used to hate the harm Quraysh did to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so when I thought they would kill him I left until I reached one of the monasteries. The people of the monastery went to their chief and told him, and he said three times: He has the right due to him. When three days passed and they saw he had not left, they went to their chief and told him. He said: Tell him: We have fulfilled the right due to you, so if you were an executor of a will, your trust has expired, and if you were one maintaining kinship, it is time for you to go to those you maintain ties with, and if you were a merchant, it is time for you to go out to your trade. He said: I was neither maintaining ties, nor a merchant, and I have no share. So they went to him and told him, and he said: He has some affair, so ask him what his affair is. They came to him and asked him, and he said: No, by Allah, except that I am in the town of Ibrahim, and my cousin claims he is a prophet, and his people harmed him, and I feared they would kill him, so I left so as not to witness that. They went to their chief and told him of my words. He said: Bring him. So I came to him and told him my story. He said: Do you fear they will kill him? I said: Yes. He said: Would you know his likeness if you saw him depicted? I said: Yes, I have known him recently. So he showed him covered pictures, uncovering one picture after another, saying: Do you recognize? And I would say: No, until he uncovered a covered picture, and I said: I have never seen anything more resembling him than this picture, as though his height, his body, and the width between his shoulders. He said: Do you fear they will kill him? He said: I think they have already finished with him. He said: By Allah, they will not kill him, and He will surely kill whoever seeks to kill him, and he is indeed a prophet, and Allah will surely make him triumphant. But his right has become due upon us, so stay as long as you wish and supplicate whatever you wish. He said: I stayed with them a while, then I said: If I obeyed them, I would return to Makkah, and I found they had expelled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Madinah. When I arrived, Quraysh came to me and said: Your affair has become clear to us and we know your case, so bring the wealth of the children with you which your father entrusted to you. I said: I would not do this until you separate my head from my body, but let me go and deliver it to them. They said: Upon you is the covenant of Allah and His pact that you shall not eat of his food. He said: I arrived at Madinah, and the news had reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I entered upon him, and he said to me among what he said: I see you are hungry, bring food. I said: I will not eat until I inform you, and if you deem I may eat, I shall eat. So I told him of what they had taken upon me. He said: Fulfil the covenant of Allah, and do not eat of our food nor drink of our drink."
"1608","178 - Jubayr ibn Iyas al-Ansari, a Badri. 1610 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding naming those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Jubayr ibn Iyas ibn Khalid ibn Makhlad ibn Zurayq."
"1609","1611 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding his naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu Zurayq: Jubayr ibn Khalid ibn Makhlad ibn Iyas."
"1610","179 - Jubayr ibn Hubab ibn al-Mundhir. 1612 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: And in the hadith of Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, regarding naming those who witnessed with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: Jubayr ibn Hubab ibn al-Mundhir."
"1611","180 - Jubayr ibn Malik al-Nawfali, killed on the day of Yamamah. 1613 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding naming those Muslims killed on the day of Yamamah, then from Quraysh: Jubayr ibn Malik, and he is Ibn Buhaynah, and he is from Banu Nawfal ibn Abd Manaf."
"1612","181 - Jubayr ibn Nawfal, not attributed. 1614 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Layth, from Isa, from Zayd ibn Artah, from Jubayr ibn Nawfal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not permitted a servant anything better than two rak'ahs or more, and righteousness scatters above the head of the servant so long as he is in prayer, and no servant draws nearer to Allah, mighty and majestic, with anything better than what came out of Him, meaning the Quran."
"1613","182 - Jundub ibn Junadah Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, may Allah be pleased with him, and he is Jundub ibn Junadah ibn Sufyan ibn Ubayd ibn Haram ibn Ghifar ibn Mulayl ibn Damrah ibn Bakr ibn Abd Manah ibn Kinanah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Mudrikah ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar ibn Nizar ibn Ma'add ibn Adnan. 1615 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr saying: The name of Abu Dharr is Jundub ibn Junadah, and it is said the name of Abu Dharr is Burayr."
"1614","1616 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Dharr: How are you, O Burayr, in a hadith we have abridged."
"1615","1617 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Rumi al-Yamami narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abu Zumayl narrated to us, from Malik ibn Marthad, from his father, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was a fourth of Islam; three men embraced Islam before me and I was the fourth. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I saw delight in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Who are you? I said: I am Jundub, a man from Banu Ghifar. It was as though he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recoiled and wished I had been from a tribe other than mine, and that was because I was from a tribe that used to rob pilgrims with their crooked staffs."
"1616","1618 - Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abdullah, from Nasr ibn Alqamah, from his brother, from Ibn Aidh, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: Abu Dharr used to say: I found myself a fourth of Islam; none embraced Islam before me except the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Bilal, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1617","1619 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr saying: Abu Dharr is Jundub ibn Junadah."
"1618","1620 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Dharr died at al-Rabadhah in the year thirty-two, and his name is Jundub ibn Junadah."
"1619","1621 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Buraydah ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Kab, that Ibn Masud came amid a mounted party and passed the funeral of Abu Dharr on the roadside, so he and his companions alighted and buried him. Abu Dharr had entered Egypt and marked out a house there."
"1620","1622 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, who said: Abu Dharr was among those who witnessed the Conquest with Amr ibn al-As."
"1621","1623 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: Asma bint Yazid narrated to me that Abu Dharr al-Ghifari used to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he finished his service he would retreat to the mosque and lie down in it, and it was his house."
"1622","1624 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Jabalah bint al-Musaffah narrated to me, from Hatib, who said: Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left nothing of what Jibril and Mikail, peace be upon them, poured into his chest except that he poured it into my chest, and I left nothing of what he poured into my chest except that I poured it into the chest of Malik ibn Damrah."
"1623","1625 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, raising the hadith to Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Dharr indeed rivals Isa son of Maryam in his worship."
"1624","1626 - And from Ibrahim al-Hajari, raising the hadith to Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at one like Isa son of Maryam in form and character, let him look at Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1625","1627 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said narrated to us, Hayyaj ibn Bistam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Dharr, who said: I am indeed the nearest of you to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Resurrection; he left the world in the same state as I leave it in, and by Allah I have innovated nothing after him, while there is none of you except that he has clung to something of it."
"1626","1628 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Layth ibn Harun al-Ukli narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, Muhammad ibn al-Walid narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: Abu Dharr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me is he who joins me upon the covenant I parted from him upon."
"1627","1629 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Asad al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Khirash, who said: I saw Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah in a black tent of his, with a plain-looking wife under him, sitting upon a piece of sackcloth. It was said to him: O Abu Dharr, you are a man none of whose children survive. He said: Praise be to Allah who takes them in the abode of perishing and stores them in the abode of permanence. They said: O Abu Dharr, if only you took a wife other than this one. He said: For me to marry a woman who lowers me is more beloved to me than a woman who raises me. They said: If only you took a mat softer than this. He said: O Allah, forgiveness; take from what You have granted whatever You will."
"1628","1630 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Husayn Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: It reached al-Harith, a man in Sham from Quraysh, that Abu Dharr was in need, so he sent him three hundred dinars. He said: He found no servant of Allah more insignificant to him than me. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever begs while having forty has importuned. And the family of Abu Dharr has forty dirhams, forty sheep and two servants."
"1629","1631 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Shubah, who said: A man came to Abu Dharr offering him maintenance, so Abu Dharr said: We have goats we milk, donkeys that carry, a freed slave woman who serves us, and a spare cloak beyond our clothing; I fear to be held to account for surplus."
"1630","Chapter: From the rare hadiths of the Musnad of Abu Dharr, may Allah have mercy on him. 1632 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: The black dog cuts off the prayer, and I think he said, and the menstruating woman. He said: So I said to Abu Dharr: What is the matter with the black dog? He said: I already asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that and he said: It is a devil."
"1631","1633 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abu Naamah, Abdullah ibn al-Samit narrated to me, that Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr, there will be rulers over you who kill the prayer; if you reach them, pray the prayer at its time and make your prayer with them supererogatory."
"1632","1634 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: My intimate friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me that whatever gold or silver is tied up is an ember upon its owner until he spends it in the path of Allah."
"1633","1635 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, Qatadah and Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The black dog and the woman cut off the prayer. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the black distinct from the white or the red? He said: The black is a devil."
"1634","1636 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"1635","1637 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban al-Sadusi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated to me, from Mutarrif, who said: A hadith from Abu Dharr used to reach me and I longed to meet him, so I met him and said: O Abu Dharr, a hadith used to reach me from you and I longed to meet you. He said: By your father, you have met me, so bring it. He said: I said: A hadith reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to you, saying: Allah, mighty and majestic, loves three and hates three. He said: I do not think I would lie against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I said: Who are these three whom Allah, mighty and majestic, loves? He said: A man who campaigns in the path of Allah, patient and seeking reward, and fights until killed, and you find him with you in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic. Then he recited this verse: Indeed Allah loves those who fight in His cause in a row as though they are a solid structure. I said: And who? He said: A man who had an evil neighbour harming him, so he bore his harm until Allah sufficed him against him by life or death. I said: And who? He said: A man who travelled with a people and they journeyed until, at the end of the night, drowsiness or sleep overcame them, so they alighted and laid their heads down, then he rose, purified himself and prayed out of desire for Allah, mighty and majestic, and desire for what is with Him. I said: And what are the three whom Allah, mighty and majestic, hates? He said: The miserly boaster, and he is in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic: Indeed Allah does not love every arrogant boaster. I said: And what is the arrogant boaster? He said: You find him in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic, the miserly arrogant. I said: And who? He said: The swearing trader or the swearing seller; he said: I do not know which of them Abu Dharr said. I said: O Abu Dharr, what is wealth? He said: A portion of sheep and camels for us. I said: O Abu Dharr, I am not asking you about this; I am asking you about hoarded wealth. He said: What is morning does not reach evening, and what is evening does not reach morning. I said: What is between you and your brothers of Quraysh? He said: By Allah, I shall not seek from them a ruling on religion nor ask them for worldly gain until I meet Allah and His Messenger; he said it three times."
"1636","1638 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best with which you change this grey hair is henna and katam."
"1637","1639 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Uththam ibn Ali mentioned - Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: I saw Ali ibn Uththam - that his father narrated to him, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Nasr, and he is Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning the Islam of Abu Dharr, and he mentioned the hadith."
"1638","1640 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, mentioning Zamzam: It is blessed; it is the food of nourishment."
"1639","1641 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, saying: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Mustalim ibn Said narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, that Abu Dharr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever ties up gold or silver and does not spend it in the path of Allah, it will be an ember on the Day of Resurrection with which he is branded."
"1640","1642 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Nuaym ibn Abdullah, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he heard Abu Zaynab, freedman of Hazim al-Ghifari, saying: I heard Abu Dharr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be ransomed for you. He said: Say: There is no might nor power except by Allah."
"1641","1643 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Nuaym ibn Abdullah, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he heard Abu Zaynab, freedman of Hazim al-Ghifari, saying: I heard Abu Dharr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr, do you say abundance of wealth is richness? I said: Yes. He said: Do you say paucity of wealth is poverty? I said: Yes. He said that three times, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is in the heart and poverty is in the heart; whoever has richness in his heart, what he meets of the world does not harm him, and whoever has poverty in his heart, what is made abundant for him in the world does not enrich him; it is only his own soul's stinginess that harms him."
"1642","1644 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan informed us, from al-Hasan, from Sasaa ibn Muawiyah, that he met Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah driving a camel of his, with two water-skins on the camel's neck and a skin-bag. He said: O Abu Dharr, what is wrong with you? He said: My deeds are mine. He said: I said: Narrate to me, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no two Muslims between whom three children die before reaching puberty except that Allah forgives them both by the bounty of His mercy upon them. He said: I said: Add to me, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever spends of his wealth a pair in the path of Allah, the keepers of Paradise will meet him, each of them calling him to what is with him. I said: A pair of what? He said: If he is a horseman, two horses; if a camel-owner, two camels; if a cattle-owner, two cows, until he counted the kinds of this sort."
"1643","1645 - Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Ahwazi and Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, Habib, Yunus and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Sasaa ibn Muawiyah, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends a pair of his wealth in the path of Allah, the keepers of Paradise will hasten to him: two camels, two horses, two sheep, two dirhams, two pairs of socks, two sandals."
"1644","1646 - Tahir ibn Isa ibn Qiras al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Amr, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym, who said: I heard Abu Dharr al-Ghifari on the pulpit saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever draws near to Allah a handspan, He draws near to him a cubit; whoever draws near to Him a cubit, Allah draws near to him a fathom; whoever comes to Allah, mighty and majestic, walking, Allah, mighty and majestic, comes to him hastening. Allah is most high and most glorious, Allah is most high and most glorious, Allah is most high and most glorious."
"1645","1647 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Fitr, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left us, and there was no bird flapping its wings in the air except that he reminded us of some knowledge from it. He said: Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing remains that draws near to Paradise and distances from the Fire except that it has been made clear to you."
"1646","1648 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani Abu Marwan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to join my kin even if they turn away, to speak the truth even if bitter, to let no blamer's blame seize me regarding Allah, to love the poor and sit with them, to look to one below me and not look to one above me, and to say often: There is no might nor power except by Allah."
"1647","1649 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Amir - and perhaps Ismail said: one of our companions - from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: My intimate friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me seven: love of the poor and drawing near them, looking to one lower than me and not looking to one above me, joining my kin even if they are harsh to me, saying often: There is no might nor power except by Allah, speaking bitter truth, letting no blamer's blame seize me regarding Allah, and not asking people for anything."
"1648","1650 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Masud narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Abu Zumayl, from Malik ibn Marthad, from his father, who said: Abu Dharr said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what saves the servant from the Fire? He said: Belief in Allah. I said: O Prophet of Allah, with belief there is action. He said: He gives of what Allah has provided him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he is poor and finds nothing to give? He said: He enjoins good and forbids evil. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he is tongue-tied, unable to enjoin good or forbid evil? He said: He makes for the unskilled. I said: What if he is unskilled, unable to make anything? He said: He aids the wronged. I said: What if he is weak, unable to aid the wronged? He said: You would leave nothing good in your companion: he withholds harm from people. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if he does that he enters Paradise? He said: No Muslim does one of these traits except that it takes his hand until it admits him to Paradise."
"1649","1651 - Ahmad ibn Anas ibn Malik al-Dimashqi al-Muqri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hisham ibn Yahya al-Ghassani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Dharr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: I advise you to fear Allah, for it is the head of your affair. I said: O Messenger of Allah, add to me. He said: Upon you is recitation of the Quran and remembrance of Allah, for that is light for you in the heavens and light on earth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, add to me. He said: Do not laugh much, for it deadens the heart and removes the light of the face. I said: O Messenger of Allah, add to me. He said: Upon you is jihad, for it is the monasticism of my nation. I said: O Messenger of Allah, add to me. He said: Upon you is silence except for good, for it repels Satan from you and aids you in your religion. I said: O Messenger of Allah, add to me. He said: Look to one below you and do not look to one above you, for it is more fitting that you not disdain Allah's blessing upon you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, add to me. He said: Join your kin even if they sever you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, add to me. He said: Do not fear any blamer's blame regarding Allah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, add to me. He said: Love for people what you love for yourself. Then he struck his hand upon my chest and said: O Abu Dharr, no intellect like prudence, no piety like restraint, and no lineage like good character."
"1650","183 - Jundub ibn Abdullah ibn Sufyan al-Bajali, then al-Alaqi, a clan of Bajilah, kunya Abu Abdullah; and it is said Jundub ibn Sufyan, and it is said Jundub ibn Khalid ibn Sufyan. 1652 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Najih, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Jundub al-Bajali, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were strong youths."
"1651","1653 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jabir ibn Kurdi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Jundub ibn Abdullah al-Bajali, who had reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1652","What al-Hasan al-Basri narrated from Jundub ibn Abdullah. 1654 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Jundub ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under Allah's protection, so beware lest Allah demand you for anything of His protection."
"1653","1655 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays dawn is under Allah's protection, and let not Allah demand you for anything of His protection."
"1654","1656 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever prays dawn is under the protection of Allah, mighty and majestic, so let not Allah demand you for anything of His protection."
"1655","1657 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us; and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, both from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer is under Allah's protection; beware, O son of Adam, lest Allah demand you for anything of His protection."
"1656","1658 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer is under Allah's protection, so let not Allah demand you for anything of His protection."
"1657","1659 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed, whoever prays the dawn prayer is under Allah's protection, so let not Allah demand you for anything of His protection."
"1658","1660 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, who said: I sat with him during the rule of al-Musab, and he said: These people have waded into blood, allied over the world and grown tall in building. I swear by Allah, only a little shall come upon you until a restive camel, two ropes and a saddle become more beloved to one of you than a great town. Know that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let not a handful of the blood of a Muslim man shed unlawfully come between one of you and Paradise while he sees its gate. Indeed, whoever prays the dawn prayer is under Allah's protection, so let not Allah demand you for anything of His protection."
"1659","1661 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Usayd ibn Asim narrated to us, Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Anbasah, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Jundub ibn Abdullah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O people, let not a handful of blood shed unjustly come between one of you and Paradise. Whoever prays the morning prayer is under Allah's protection; O son of Adam, let not Allah demand you for anything of His protection."
"1660","1662 - Musa ibn Harun, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, saying: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Jundub ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is able not to let a handful of blood he sheds, as though slaughtering a chicken, come between him and Paradise - whenever he advances to a gate of Paradise it comes between him and it - and whoever of you is able not to admit into his belly except what is wholesome, for the first of man to putrefy is his belly."
"1661","1663 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Jundub; and Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Adam met Musa, peace be upon them. Musa said: Are you Adam whom Allah created with His hand, settled in His Paradise and made His angels prostrate to you, then you did what you did and expelled your offspring from Paradise? Adam, peace be upon him, said: Are you Musa whom Allah chose with His message, spoke to you and brought you near in secret converse? He said: Yes. Then am I older or the remembrance? He said: Rather the remembrance. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa, so Adam overcame Musa, so Adam overcame Musa."
"1662","1664 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, Jundub ibn Abdullah al-Bajali narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man among those before you was wounded and grew impatient with it, so he took a knife and cut his hand with it, and the blood did not staunch until he died. Allah, mighty and majestic, said: My servant hastened himself to Me; I have forbidden Paradise to you."
"1663","1665 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hadd of the sorcerer is a stroke with the sword."
"1664","1666 - Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Sayyar narrated to us, Khalid al-Abd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The hadd of the sorcerer is a stroke with the sword."
"1665","Abu Abdullah al-Jushami from Jundub. 1667 - Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Jurayri narrated to me, from Abu Abdullah al-Jushami, Jundub narrated to us, who said: A Bedouin came, made his mount kneel, hobbled it, then prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam, he went to his mount, released its hobble, mounted it, then called out: O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad and associate no one in our mercy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you say? Is he more astray or his camel? He has restricted a vast mercy. Allah, mighty and majestic, created a hundred mercies, then sent down of them one mercy by which creatures show affection to one another - its jinn, humans and beasts - and with Him are ninety-nine. Do you say he is more astray or his camel?"
"1666","Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi from Jundub. 1668 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ubaydah al-Tammar narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hadrami, from Abu al-Sawwar, from Jundub ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer has the protection of Allah, or as he said. And it reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever violates my protection, I shall be his adversary, and whomever I oppose, I overcome him."
"1667","1669 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ubaydah al-Tammar narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hadrami, from Abu al-Sawwar, from Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qiblah and eats our slaughtered meat, that is the Muslim; he has the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger."
"1668","1670 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, al-Hadrami narrated to me, from Abu al-Sawwar, from Jundub ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he sent a party and appointed over them Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah or Ubaydah. When he went to depart, he wept out of longing for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sat down, and he appointed Abdullah ibn Jahsh over them in his place. He wrote him a letter and ordered him not to read the letter until he reached such-and-such place, and said: Do not compel any of your companions to march with you. When he read the letter he said: We hear and obey Allah and His Messenger. He told them the news and read the letter to them; two men returned and the rest went on. They met Ibn al-Hadrami and killed him, not knowing whether that day was of Rajab or Jumada. The polytheists said to the Muslims: You killed in the sacred month. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: They ask you about the sacred month, fighting therein. The verse. Some of them said: If they incurred no sin, they have no reward. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: Indeed those who believed and those who emigrated and strove in the cause of Allah, those hope for the mercy of Allah, and Allah is forgiving, merciful."
"1669","Abu Mijlaz Lahiq ibn Humayd from Jundub. 1671 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us; and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, both from Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, from Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed under a blind banner, aiding partisanship and angering for partisanship, his death is a death of ignorance."
"1670","Abu Imran al-Jawni from Jundub. 1672 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib and al-Hasan ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever speaks about the Quran by his opinion, even if right, has erred."
"1671","1673 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan and Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us; and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us; and Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, Sallam ibn Abi Muti narrated to us, all from Abu Imran, from Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Gather upon the Quran so long as you agree upon it; when you differ over it, stand up."
"1672","1674 - Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa al-Nahwi narrated to us, Abu Imran narrated to us, from Jundub ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the Quran so long as your hearts agree upon it; when they differ, stand up."
"1673","1675 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Furafisah, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather upon the Quran so long as you agree upon it; when you differ, stand up."
"1674","1676 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Abu Imran, who said: I asked Jundub ibn Abdullah: Did you press the non-Arabs into service? He said: We used to press them from village to village to guide us on the road, then we would release them."
"1675","1677 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, who said: I said to Jundub ibn Abdullah: I pledged allegiance to Ibn al-Zubayr to fight the people of Sham. He said: Perhaps you will say: Jundub gave me a ruling, and I follow. He said: I said: I do not intend that, but I seek your ruling so you may rule for me. He said: Then he said: Ransom with your wealth. I said: It will not be accepted from me. Jundub said: I was at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a strong youth, and so-and-so told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slain will come on the Day of Resurrection with his killer clinging to him, and Allah, mighty and majestic, will say: For what did you kill him? He will say: For the kingdom of so-and-so. So fear Allah lest you be that man."
"1676","1678 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Najih; and Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Bistam ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Najih narrated to us, from Abu Imran, from Jundub, who said: We were with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as strong youths, and we learned belief before we learned the Quran, then we learned the Quran and increased in belief thereby. Today you learn the Quran before belief."
"1677","1679 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan and Huraym ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, saying: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Imran, from Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man said: By Allah, Allah will not forgive so-and-so. Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Who is he who swears upon Me that I shall not forgive so-and-so? I have forgiven so-and-so and annulled your deed."
"1678","1680 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Imran narrated to us, from Jundub, that a man swore that Allah would not forgive so-and-so. Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or to a prophet, that it is in the station of a sin, so let him resume deeds."
"1679","Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi from Jundub. 1681 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ali ibn Sulayman al-Kalbi narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to me, from Abu Tamimah, from Jundub ibn Abdullah al-Azdi, Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I set out, he and I, to Basrah until we came to a place called Bayt al-Miskin, which is from Basrah like al-Thawiyyah from Kufah. He said: Did you use to study the Quran with anyone? I said: Yes. He said: When we come to Basrah, bring them to me. So I brought him Salih ibn Musarrih, Abu Bilal, Najdah and Nafi ibn al-Azraq, who were in my view that day among the best of Basrah's people. He began narrating to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Jundub said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the scholar who teaches people good and forgets himself is like the lamp that lights for people and burns itself. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not a handful of the blood of a Muslim he shed unjustly come between one of you and Paradise while he looks at its gates. He said: The people spoke, mentioning enjoining good and forbidding evil, while he was silent listening to them. Then he said: I have never seen like today a people more deserving of salvation, if they are truthful."
"1680","1682 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Tarif Abu Tamimah, who said: I witnessed Safwan and Jundub and his companions while he was enjoining them, and they said to him: Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard him saying: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him on the Day of Resurrection, and I think he said: And whoever causes hardship, Allah will cause hardship upon him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1681","Anas ibn Sirin from Jundub. 1683 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, who said: I heard Jundub ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of Allah, mighty and majestic, so let not Allah demand you for anything of His protection; for whoever He demands for anything of His protection, He overtakes him and casts him into the fire of Hell."
"1682","1684 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jabir ibn Kurdi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Jundub, who had reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"1683","Safwan ibn Muhriz al-Mazini from Jundub. 1685 - Sulayman ibn al-Muafa ibn Sulayman and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Jundub ibn Abdullah, that he passed by people reciting the Quran and said: Let these not deceive you; they recite the Quran today and will strike with swords tomorrow. Then he said: Bring me a group of Quran reciters, and let them be elders. So I brought him Nafi ibn al-Azraq, Mirdas Abu Bilal, and a group with them, six or eight. When we entered upon Jundub, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The example of one who teaches people good and forgets himself is like the lamp that lights for people and burns itself. Whoever shows off to people with his knowledge, Allah will show him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah will make them hear of him. Know that the first of one of you to putrefy when he dies is his belly, so let him admit into his belly only what is wholesome. Whoever of you is able not to let a handful of blood come between him and Paradise, let him do so."
"1684","Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Jundub. 1686 - Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, Jundub narrated to us that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) five days before his death saying: I had among you brothers and friends, and I absolve myself to Allah of having an intimate friend among you. Had I taken an intimate friend from my nation I would have taken Abu Bakr as intimate friend. My Lord, mighty and majestic, has taken me as intimate friend as He took Ibrahim as intimate friend. Indeed those before you used to take the graves of their prophets and righteous as mosques, so do not take graves as mosques, for I forbid you that."
"1685","Al-Walid ibn Muslim from Jundub. 1687 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Jundub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you seeks permission three times and is not permitted, let him return."
"1686","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Jundub. 1688 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, and Waki, from Misar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jundub, who said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"1687","1689 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Muhayyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Jundub, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"1688","1690 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Jundub, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"1689","1691 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated to us; and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jundub ibn Sufyan al-Bajali, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"1690","1692 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya al-Abdasi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"1691","1693 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abu Yaqub al-Thaqafi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jundub, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"1692","1694 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, who said: I heard Jundub saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"1693","1695 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Jundub ibn Sufyan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The best prayer after the obligatory is prayer in the depth of the night, and the best fasting after Ramadan is the month of Allah which you call al-Muharram."
"1694","Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Jundub. 1696 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Jundub saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and I heard no one saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, other than him. He said: I drew near him and heard him saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him, and whoever makes a show, Allah will make a show of him."
"1695","1697 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us, Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Jundub ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him; whoever makes a show, Allah will make a show of him; and whoever has two tongues in the world, Allah will make for him two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"1696","1698 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Hamid ibn Yahya narrated to us; and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us; and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Harb; and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Amr al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, the truthful trustworthy al-Walid ibn Harb narrated to us, who said: I heard Salamah ibn Kuhayl saying: I heard none who heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Jundub, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him, and whoever makes a show, Allah will make a show of him."
"1697","1699 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Jundub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever makes a show, Allah will make a show of him, and whoever shows off, Allah will expose him."
"1698","1700 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to me, Salamah ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Jundub, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him, and whoever makes a show, Allah will make a show of him."
"1699","1701 - Salamah ibn Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba and its giver."
"1700","1702 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hamid ibn Adam al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Jundub ibn Sufyan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant conceals a secret but Allah clothes him with its garment: if good, good, and if evil, evil."
"1701","Al-Aswad ibn Qays from Jundub. 1703 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, who said: I heard Jundub saying: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking, a stone struck him and he stumbled and his finger bled. He said: Are you but a finger that bled, and in the path of Allah you suffered."
"1702","1704 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub ibn Sufyan, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking, a stone struck his finger. He said: It bled. He said: You are but a finger that bled, and in the path of Allah you suffered."
"1703","1705 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us; and Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave and his finger was injured. He said: Are you but a finger that bled, and in the path of Allah you suffered."
"1704","1706 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub, that a stone struck the finger of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it bled. He said: Are you but a finger that bled, and in the path of Allah you suffered."
"1705","1707 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from al-Aswad, from Jundub, who said: A stone struck the foot of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it bled. He said: Are you but a finger that bled, and in the path of Allah you suffered."
"1706","1708 - Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Shahin al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub, who said: The finger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bled in one of the battle scenes. He said: You are but a finger that bled, and in the path of Allah you suffered."
"1707","1709 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, who said: I heard Jundub saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill and did not rise for a night or two. A woman came to him and said: O Muhammad, I see your devil has left you. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: By the morning brightness, and the night when it covers, your Lord has not forsaken you nor does He hate you."
"1708","1710 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Aswad, who said: I heard Jundub; and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub ibn Sufyan, who said: Jibril was withheld from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so one of his paternal cousins' daughters said: I see your companion has forsaken you. He said: Then was sent down: By the morning brightness, and the night when it covers, your Lord has not forsaken you nor does He hate you. And the wording is that of the hadith of Amr ibn Marzuq."
"1709","1711 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Aswad narrated to us, from Jundub ibn Sufyan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill and did not rise for two nights or three. A woman said: O Muhammad, I hope your devil has left you; we have not seen him near you for two or three nights. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: By the morning brightness, and the night when it covers, your Lord has not forsaken you nor does He hate you."
"1710","1712 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated to us, from Jundub, who said: Jibril tarried from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the polytheists said: Muhammad has been forsaken. Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down upon His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your Lord has not forsaken you nor does He hate you, and the Hereafter is better for you than the first, and your Lord will give you and you will be pleased."
"1711","1713 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us; and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Aswad, who said: I heard Jundub saying: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray then address, saying: Whoever slaughtered before praying, let him slaughter and replace it; whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter in the name of Allah."
"1712","1714 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, Jundub ibn Sufyan narrated to me, who said: I witnessed al-Adha with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He had only prayed and finished his prayer when he saw sacrificial meat slaughtered before he finished his prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever slaughtered his sacrifice before praying, let him slaughter another in its place; whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter in the name of Allah."
"1713","1715 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us; and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated to us, from Jundub ibn Sufyan, who said: I witnessed sacrifice with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He led the people in prayer, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer he saw sheep slaughtered. He said: Whoever slaughtered before the prayer, let him slaughter a sheep in its place; whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter in the name of Allah."
"1714","1716 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Awanah, Sharik and Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub ibn Sufyan, who said: I witnessed al-Adha with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He saw people who had slaughtered before the prayer. He said: Whoever slaughtered before the prayer, let him repeat the slaughter; whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter upon the name of Allah."
"1715","1717 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad, from Jundub, who said: I witnessed the Eid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He learned that people had slaughtered before the prayer, so he addressed the people and said: Whoever slaughtered before the prayer, let him repeat his slaughter; whoever has not, let him slaughter upon the name of Allah."
"1716","1718 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Musa ibn Sufyan al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from al-Aswad, from Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and said: Whoever slaughtered his sacrifice before the prayer, let him slaughter another in its place; whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter in the name of Allah."
"1717","1719 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Umar ibn Ziyad al-Alhani narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub, who said: A tree struck the finger of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it bled. He said: Are you but a finger that bled, and in the path of Allah you suffered. Then he was carried and placed upon a bed woven with palm fronds or strips, with a leather cushion stuffed with fibre under his head. The strip left a mark on his side. Umar ibn al-Khattab came and wept. He said: What makes you weep? He said: O Messenger of Allah, Kisra and Qaysar sit upon beds of gold and wear brocade and silk. He said: Are you not pleased that they have the world and you have the Hereafter."
"1718","1720 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Aswad, from Jundub, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love night vigil prayer."
"1719","Abu Sahl al-Fazari from Jundub. 1721 - Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Yazid al-Sami al-Basri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Ghudani narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Sahl al-Fazari, from his father, from Jundub, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met his Companions, he would not shake their hands until he greeted them."
"1720","1722 - Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Yazid al-Sami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ubaydullah al-Ghudani narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Sahl al-Fazari, from his father, from Jundub, who said: We travelled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey. People came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we forgot the prayer and did not pray until the sun rose. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution and pray. Then he said: This is not forgetfulness; this is from Satan. When one of you takes his bed at night, let him say: In the name of Allah, I seek refuge in Allah from Satan the accursed."
"1721","Shahr ibn Hawshab from Jundub. 1723 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us; and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, who said: Jundub ibn Sufyan, a man from Bajilah, narrated to me, saying: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bearer of glad tidings came from his detachment, telling him of the victory Allah granted his detachment and the conquest Allah opened for them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, while we were pursuing the people after Allah had routed them, I caught up with a man with the sword. When he sensed the sword would strike him, while running and saying: I am a Muslim, I am a Muslim. He said: So you killed him? He said: O Messenger of Allah, he only sought refuge. He said: Why did you not split open his heart and see whether he was truthful or lying? He said: Had I split open his heart, what would my knowledge be, for his heart is but a piece of flesh? He said: You know not what is in his heart, nor did you believe his tongue. He said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He said: I shall not seek forgiveness for you. He said: That man died and they buried him, and in the morning he was upon the face of the earth. Then they buried him and in the morning he was upon the face of the earth, three times. When they saw that, they were ashamed and disgraced by what befell him, so they carried him and cast him into a ravine among those ravines."
"1722","1724 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us; and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, Jundub ibn Sufyan narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be after me trials like pieces of the dark night; a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and a disbeliever in the evening and a believer in the morning. A man among the Muslims said: What shall we do then, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Enter your houses and obscure your mention. A man said: What if one of us is entered upon in his house? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him hold his hand and be the slain servant of Allah, not the killing servant of Allah. For a man will be in the fold of Islam, then consume his brother's wealth, shed his blood, disobey his Lord, disbelieve in his Creator, and the Fire becomes due for him."
"1723","184 - Jundub ibn Kab al-Azdi, and his Companionship has been disputed. 1725 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim Abu Mamar al-Qatii narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, that a sorcerer used to perform before al-Walid ibn Uqbah, taking a sword, slaughtering himself and doing such, and it did not harm him. Jundub rose to the sword, took it and struck his neck. Then he recited: Do you come to sorcery while you see."
"1724","185 - Jundub ibn Makith al-Juhani. 1726 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq; and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Yaqub ibn Utbah narrated to me, from Muslim ibn Abdullah al-Juhani, from Jundub ibn Abdullah al-Juhani; and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Jafar ibn Mihran al-Sabbak narrated to us, Abd al-Ala al-Sami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Utbah, from Muslim ibn Abdullah, from Jundub ibn Abdullah al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ghalib ibn Abdullah al-Kalbi, Kalb Awf ibn Layth, in a detachment in which I was. He ordered him to launch a raid upon Banu al-Mulawwih at al-Kadid. He said: We went out until, when we were at Qudayd, we met al-Harith ibn al-Barsa al-Laythi and seized him. He said: I came only to embrace Islam; I set out seeking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We said: If you are a Muslim, a night's bond will not harm you; if you are otherwise, we shall secure you. So we bound him, then left over him a small black man who was with us, saying to him: If he resists you, cut off his head. Then we came to al-Kadid at sunset. We were in a quarter of the valley, and my companions sent me as their scout to a hill overlooking the settlement. He said: I climbed it until, when I was on its top and looked at the people, I lay flat. By Allah, I was upon it looking when a man came out of his tent and said to his wife: By Allah, I see a darkness I did not see at the start of the day; look into your vessels lest the dogs have dragged some of them. She looked and said: By Allah, I miss nothing of my vessels. He said: Give me my bow. She gave him a bow with two arrows. He said: He shot an arrow, and by Allah it did not miss my side. I pulled it out and stayed still. Then he shot the other and placed it in my shoulder. I pulled it out and stayed still. He said to his wife: Had it been a moving thing it would have moved by now; my two arrows have struck it. When morning comes, seek them and take them, lest the dogs waste them. Then he entered. When the people's livestock of camels and sheep returned at evening, and they milked, supped and settled, we launched the raid upon them, killed and drove off the sheep. Then we directed them onward. The people's cry went out among them, and reinforcements came to them, pursuing us until we passed by Ibn al-Barsa, and we took him with us along with our companion we had left. The people caught up with us until we saw them, with only the valley between us and them, facing from one side and pursuing from the other side, when Allah brought it from where He willed: rain we had not seen before, which none could cross. I saw them standing looking at us while we drove them on, none of them able to reach us, until we drove them up. I shall never forget the words of a rajiz among the Muslims driving them at their heels:"
"1725","186 - Jundub ibn Najiyah. 1727 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Rajjani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Abdullah, a shaykh of Aslam, from Jundub ibn Najiyah, or Najiyah ibn Jundub, who said: When we were at al-Ghamim, news reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Quraysh that they had sent Khalid ibn al-Walid with a detachment of cavalry to meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked meeting him, and he was merciful toward them. He said: Which man will divert us from the road? I said: I, may my father be for you. He took them by a road in which there were barren rugged lands and eagles, and the land levelled for us until he brought him down at al-Hudaybiyah, which was depleted. He overturned an arrow, or his arrow, from his quiver into it, then spat into it, then supplicated, and its springs gushed until I say, or we say: Had we wished we could have scooped with our hands."
"1726","187 - Jundub ibn Humamah al-Dawsi, killed on the day of Ajnadayn. 1728 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding naming those Muslims martyred on the day of Ajnadayn: Jundub ibn Humamah al-Dawsi, ally of Banu Umayyah ibn Abd Shams."
"1727","1729 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding naming those martyred on the day of Ajnadayn: Jundub ibn Amr ibn Humamah al-Dawsi, ally of Banu Umayyah ibn Abd Shams."
"1728","Chapter: Those named Jabir. Jabir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Haram ibn Thalabah al-Ansari, kunya Abu Abdullah, and it is said Abu Abd al-Rahman. 1730 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding naming the companions of al-Aqabah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar: Jabir ibn Abdullah ibn Haram ibn Kab ibn Ghanm ibn Kab ibn Salamah."
"1729","1731 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding naming those who witnessed al-Aqabah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar: Jabir ibn Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Amr."
"1730","1732 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Jabir ibn Abdullah died in the year seventy-eight, aged eighty-five, kunya Abu Abd al-Rahman."
"1731","1733 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hisham ibn Bahram al-Madaini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, saying: Jabir ibn Abdullah died in the year seventy-eight. He said: And Kharijah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, saying: I saw a cloak upon his bier, and Aban ibn Uthman, governor of Madinah, prayed over him. Jabir ibn Abdullah died aged ninety-four, kunya Abu Abdullah, and his sight had gone, may Allah have mercy on him."
"1732","1734 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, from al-Haytham ibn Adi, who said: Jabir ibn Abdullah perished in the year seventy-four."
"1733","1735 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini narrated to us, Abu Zayd ibn Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, saying: Jabir ibn Abdullah died in the year seventy-nine."
"1734","1736 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, from Man ibn Isa, who said: Jabir ibn Abdullah died in the year sixty."
"1735","1737 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr saying: Jabir ibn Abdullah died in the year ninety-eight, and his sight had gone."
"1736","1738 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to me, Hanzalah ibn Amr al-Ansari narrated to us, from Abu al-Huwayrith, who said: Jabir ibn Abdullah perished and we attended his door in Banu Salamah. When his bier came out of his room, Hasan ibn Hasan was between the two posts of the bier. Al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf ordered him to come out from between the posts, but he refused them until they contended with him. The sons of Jabir asked him to come out, so he came out. Al-Hajjaj came until he stood between the posts until it was laid down, and he prayed over him. Then he came to the grave, and Hasan ibn Hasan ibn ... had descended into his grave. Al-Hajjaj ordered him to come out, but he refused. The sons of Jabir said: By Allah. So he came out, and al-Hajjaj leapt into the pit until it was finished."
"1737","1739 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, who said: We came to Jabir ibn Abdullah after his sight had gone."
"1738","1740 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Uthman ibn Ubaydullah, who said: I saw Jabir ibn Abdullah dyeing with yellow, and he witnessed al-Aqabah."
"1739","1741 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of al-Aqabah. Jabir said: My maternal uncle brought me out while I could not throw a stone."
"1740","1742 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Umar ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Yasin al-Zayyat, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in thirteen expeditions."
"1741","And from the rare (gharib) narrations of Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with him, 1743 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar; Jabir ibn Abdillah informed me, he said: Some people saw a fire in a graveyard and came to it, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hand me your companion - and it was the man who used to raise his voice in remembrance (of Allah)."
"1742","1744 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the perfection of prayer is the straightening of the row."
"1743","1745 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, he kept his arms apart until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"1744","1746 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Salih ibn Abdillah al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Amir narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, their blood and their wealth are protected from me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1745","1747 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is granted a life-tenancy (umra), it belongs to him and to his descendants."
"1746","1748 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Ata, from his father - as Abu Bakr held - from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fresh dates for dry dates, and grapes for raisins, but he permitted araya sales; and araya is when a bedouin comes to a cousin of his or a man of his household and he assigns to him one palm tree or two palm trees before they ripen, while he intends to go out (on a journey) - then there is no harm in his selling it for dry dates."
"1747","1749 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, Abthar narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Ata, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent condiment vinegar is."
"1748","1750 - Khayr ibn Arafa al-Misri narrated to us, Urwa ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am Ahmad, and I am Muhammad, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet Allah will gather the people, and I am al-Mahi by whom Allah will efface disbelief; and when the Day of Resurrection comes, the Banner of Praise will be with me, and I shall be the leader of the Messengers and the bearer of their intercession."
"1749","1751 - Khayr ibn Arafa al-Misri narrated to us, Urwa narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is not in the seven heavens a foot-space, nor a span, nor a palm, except that in it there is an angel standing, or an angel bowing, or an angel prostrating; and when the Day of Resurrection comes, they will all say: Glory be to You, we did not worship You as You deserve to be worshipped - except that we never associated anything with You."
"1750","1752 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Khaliq ibn Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard Busr ibn Abdillah mentioning from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the dhimmis (protected non-Muslim subjects) are wronged, power becomes the power of the enemy; when adultery becomes abundant, captivity becomes abundant; and when homosexuality becomes abundant, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, lifts His hand from the creation and does not care in which valley they perish."
"1751","1753 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, from Malik ibn Anas, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: My eyes saw and my ears heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Jirana, with silver in the garment of Bilal, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taking handfuls of it for the people and giving them; then a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, be just! He said: Woe to you - who will be just if I am not just? You are ruined and lost if I am not just. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Let me, O Messenger of Allah, kill this hypocrite. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbid that people should say that I kill my companions. This man and his companions recite the Quran and it does not pass their throats; they pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the game."
"1752","1754 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Makhlad narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muadh, I am sending you to a people of the Scripture; if you are asked about the Milky Way in the sky, say: It is the saliva of a serpent beneath the Throne."
"1753","1755 - Abu Dharr Harun ibn Sulayman al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends evil for a servant, He makes bricks and clay look attractive to him until he builds."
"1754","1756 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafs al-Attar narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi Hafs, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: On the day of the expedition of Taif, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, in private conversation for a long part of the day; so Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: O Messenger of Allah, your private conversation with Ali has been long since today. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not I who conversed with him privately, but Allah who conversed with him."
"1755","1757 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Ammar al-Duhni narrated to me, from his father, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: My uncle Jadd ibn Qays carried me among seventy riders who came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with his uncle al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he said: O uncle, take a pledge on behalf of your nephews. Then the seventy said: O Muhammad, ask for your Lord and for yourself whatever you wish. He said: As for what I ask of you for my Lord - that you worship Him and associate nothing with Him; and as for what I ask of you for myself - that you protect me as you protect yourselves."
"1756","1758 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was black."
"1757","1759 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the sea: Its water is purifying and its dead (animals) are lawful."
"1758","1760 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in a detachment with no provisions except a bag of dates, and he appointed Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah over us; he would give us a handful of dates until we had our morning meal, and he would give us one date at a time. Then the sea cast up a beast, so we ate from it; then Abu Ubayda ordered a rib (of it) to be set up in an arch, then he ordered a man who mounted a camel and passed riding beneath it on the camel."
"1759","1761 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, in marfu form, he said: Dates and unripe dates (busr) are wine (i.e. when used to make intoxicants)."
"1760","Jabir ibn Khalid al-Ansari, a Badri. 1762 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abi al-Aswad, from Urwa: Concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then from Banu Dinar ibn al-Najjar: Jabir ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Ashhal ibn Haritha ibn Dinar."
"1761","1763 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then from Banu Dinar ibn al-Najjar: Jabir ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Ashhal, he left no descendants."
"1762","190 - Jabir ibn Abdillah ibn Khalid ibn Riyab al-Ansari, a Badri. 1764 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abi al-Aswad, from Urwa: Concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Jabir ibn Abdillah ibn Riyab ibn Numan ibn Sinan."
"1763","1765 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then Banu Ubayd ibn Adi: Jabir ibn Abdillah ibn Ziyad ibn Numan."
"1764","1766 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intended to manifest His religion and honour His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and fulfil His promise, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the season in which he met the group of the Ansar - and they were, as they claim, six, among them Jabir ibn Abdillah ibn Riyab."
"1765","And what Jabir ibn Abdillah ibn Riyab narrated. 1767 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from al-Wazi ibn Nafi, from Abi Salama, from Jabir ibn Riyab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril passed by me while I was praying, and he smiled at me, so I smiled back at him."
"1766","1768 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from al-Wazi ibn Nafi, from Abi Salama, from Jabir ibn Riyab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Khadija: Jibril came to me and said: Give Khadija glad tidings of a house of hollowed pearl, in which there is no noise and no toil."
"1767","191 - Jabir ibn Atik al-Ansari, a Badri, also called Jabr. 1769 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abi al-Aswad, from Urwa: Concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then from Banu Muawiya ibn Malik ibn Awf ibn Amr ibn Awf: Jabr ibn Atik ibn al-Harith ibn Qays ibn Habshiyya ibn al-Harith ibn Umayya. Thus Urwa said: Ibn Hubaysha, while Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: Ibn Haysha."
"1768","1770 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then from Banu Muawiya ibn Malik ibn Awf: Jabir ibn Atik ibn al-Harith."
"1769","1771 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Atik died in the year sixty-one, at the age of seventy-one."
"1770","And what Jabir ibn Atik narrated. 1772 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from Jabir ibn Atik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Among protective jealousy (ghayra) is that which Allah loves, and among it is that which Allah hates. As for the jealousy Allah loves, it is jealousy in a matter of suspicion; and as for the jealousy Allah hates, it is jealousy where there is no suspicion. And among pride (khuyala) is that which Allah loves and that which Allah hates: as for the pride Allah loves, it is a man showing pride in himself when giving charity and when fighting; and as for the pride Allah hates, it is his pride in tyranny and immorality."
"1771","1773 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi narrated to me, Ibn Atik narrated to me, that his father narrated to him - and his father was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among jealousy is that which Allah loves and among it is that which Allah hates; and among pride is that which Allah loves and among it is that which Allah hates. As for the jealousy Allah loves, it is jealousy in a matter of suspicion; and the jealousy Allah hates is jealousy where there is no suspicion. And the pride Allah loves is a man showing pride in himself for Allah when fighting; and the pride Allah hates is pride in tyranny or in immorality."
"1772","1774 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among jealousy is that which Allah loves, and among it is that which Allah hates. As for what Allah loves of jealousy, it is jealousy in a matter of suspicion; and as for the jealousy Allah hates, it is jealousy where there is no suspicion. And as for the pride Allah loves, it is a man showing pride in himself when fighting; and as for the pride Allah hates, it is a man showing pride in tyranny and immorality."
"1773","1775 - Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, Ibn Jabir ibn Atik narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - similarly."
"1774","1776 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Jabir ibn Atik al-Ansari, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same."
"1775","1777 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same."
"1776","1778 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, (h) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Atik, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever goes out striving in the way of Allah - then he joined together his three fingers, then said: And where are the strivers? - then falls from his mount and dies, his reward is due upon Allah; or dies a natural death, his reward is due upon Allah; and whoever is killed outright (qasan) has earned the (final) return."
"1777","1779 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abdillah ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from Atik ibn al-Harith ibn Atik - who is the grandfather of Abdullah ibn Abdillah, the father of his mother - that he informed him that Jabir ibn Atik informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit Abdullah ibn Thabit, and found him overcome (by death); so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out to him and he did not answer him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi rajiun and said: We have been overcome regarding you, O Abu al-Rabi. Then the women shrieked and wept, and Ibn Atik began to quieten them; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave them; when the obligation occurs, let no weeping woman weep. They said: What is the obligation, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When he dies. His daughter said: By Allah, I had hoped you would be a martyr, for you had prepared your equipment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has granted him his reward according to his intention; and what do you count as martyrdom? They said: Being killed in the way of Allah. He said: Martyrdom is seven besides being killed in the way of Allah: the one who dies of plague is a martyr, the drowned is a martyr, the one with pleurisy is a martyr, the one with abdominal illness is a martyr, the one burned is a martyr, the one who dies under rubble is a martyr, and the woman who dies in childbirth (bi-jumin) is a martyr."
"1778","1780 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, (h) and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, all said: Waki narrated to us, from Abi al-Umays, from Abdullah ibn Abdillah ibn Jabr, from his father, from his grandfather Jabr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited him in his illness; then someone said: We had hoped his death would be killing in the way of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the martyrs of my nation would be few: the one killed in the way of Allah is a martyr, the one with abdominal illness is a martyr, the one with plague is a martyr, the drowned is a martyr, the burned is a martyr, and the one with pleurisy is a martyr."
"1779","1781 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Shayban, from Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Abdillah ibn Jabr, from Mabad ibn Jabr, from Jabir ibn Atik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked three things in the mosque of Banu Muawiya, and was granted two and refused one: he asked Him not to destroy his nation by hunger, nor to grant an enemy victory over them - and he was granted that; and he asked Him not to set their strife among themselves - and he was refused that."
"1780","1782 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid narrated to us, Abu Sufyan ibn Jabir ibn Atik narrated to me, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever cuts off the wealth of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah forbids Paradise to him and makes the Fire obligatory for him. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something small? He said: Even if it is a tooth-stick (siwak)."
"1781","1783 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, my maternal uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Salim narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, from Abi Sufyan ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts off the wealth of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah forbids Paradise to him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something small? He said: Even if it is a twig of arak."
"1782","1784 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid informed me, from Abi Sufyan, from Abi Sufyan ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same; and the narration of Ibn Wahb ends at: Allah forbids Paradise to him."
"1783","192 - Jabir ibn Umayr al-Ansari. 1785 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, (h) and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abi Abd al-Rahim, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: I saw Jabir ibn Abdillah and Jabir ibn Umayr al-Ansari shooting arrows; one of them tired and sat down, so the other said to him: You have grown lazy! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Everything that is not of the remembrance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is diversion or heedlessness, except four qualities: a man walking between the two targets, training his horse, playing with his family, and learning to swim."
"1784","193 - Jabir ibn Usama al-Juhani. 1786 - Masada ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usama ibn Zayd, from Muadh ibn Abdillah ibn Khubayb, from Jabir ibn Usama al-Juhani, he said: I met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his Companions at the market, and I asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah where he intended to go. They said: He is marking out a mosque for your people. So I returned and found my people standing; I said: What is the matter with you? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marked out a mosque for us and planted a piece of wood in the qibla direction, setting it up there."
"1785","1787 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muadh ibn Abdillah ibn Khubayb, from Jabir ibn Usama al-Juhani, he said: I went to the market and met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his Companions, and I asked them: Where does he intend to go? They said: He is marking out a mosque for your people. So I returned and found my people standing; I said: What is your affair? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marked out a mosque for us with his foot and planted a piece of wood in the qibla direction, planting it there."
"1786","Jabir ibn Samura al-Suwai, his kunya is Abu Khalid, also said to be Abu Abdillah; his lineage. 1788 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Salm ibn Junada narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: Jabir ibn Samura ibn Junada ibn Jundub ibn Hujayr ibn Riyab ibn Khubayb ibn Suwata ibn Amir; and the kunya of Jabir is Abu Abdillah; and the mother of Jabir ibn Samura is Khalida bint Abi Waqqas, the sister of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas."
"1787","And from his reports. 1789 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, both said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than a hundred times."
"1788","Mention of his death and who prayed over him. 1790 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Salm ibn Junada narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: Jabir ibn Samura died, and Amr ibn Hurayth prayed over him."
"1789","What Jabir ibn Samura narrated. Chapter: Amir al-Shabi from Jabir ibn Samura. 1791 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, (h) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, both from Ibn Awn, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This religion will remain mighty and protected until twelve caliphs - then he said a word; so I said to my father: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1790","1792 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam will remain mighty until twelve caliphs."
"1791","1793 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same."
"1792","1794 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I was with my father at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: There will be for this nation twelve custodians (qayyim), those who forsake them will not harm them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whispered a word I did not hear; so I said to my father: What is the word the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whispered? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1793","1795 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us one day, and I heard him saying: This religion will remain mighty, protected, and triumphant over those who oppose it, until twelve rule - all of them... Then the people made noise and spoke, so I did not understand his saying after: all of them. So I said to my father: O my father, what is after his saying: all of them? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1794","1796 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage saying: This affair will remain triumphant over those who oppose it; no opponent nor dissenter will harm it, until twelve caliphs from Quraysh pass."
"1795","1797 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughira, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I heard him saying: The affair of this nation will remain triumphant until twelve stand - and he said a word that was hidden from me; and my father was sitting closer to him than me, so I said: What did he say? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1796","1798 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Qazaa narrated to us, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my father, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The affair of this nation will remain upright until there are twelve caliphs; then he said a hidden word, so I said to my father: What did he say? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1797","1799 - Al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Halim al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Abdillah narrated to us, (h) and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us, Umar ibn Abdillah ibn Razin narrated to us, both from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Said ibn Amr ibn Ashwa, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samura al-Suwai, he said: I came with my father to the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was addressing; I heard him saying: There will be after me twelve caliphs - then he lowered his voice and I did not know what he said, so I said to my father: What is he saying? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1798","1800 - Abu Habib Zayd ibn al-Muhtadi al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Imran ibn Sulayman, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage saying: The affair of this nation will remain calm against those who oppose it, until there are over you twelve commanders - then he spoke a word I did not hear, so I asked my father - who was closer to him than me: What did he say? He said: He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1799","1801 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Dawud al-Awdi, from Amir, and from his father, both said: We heard Jabir ibn Samura saying: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: This affair will remain standing until twelve commanders pass. He said: And he shortened a word I did not hear. He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent, I said to my father Samura: What is the word he shortened? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1800","Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas from Jabir ibn Samura. 1802 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, both said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, bestows a blessing upon a servant, let him begin with himself and his household."
